x=Ká¢:´óº(Ω˘∫?ï∆º∞ºÒ„©ºæt␀º¡⁄-<{¢ªÚ]4<Ÿ];≈]äºªÂ8<™˛gº”ò‰ºz=ÉuØºﬁΩºvì∑;˝.hº*ŒΩª
¥ºZ◊9<÷'¨ªï÷ä<—®Hª,<›:.0r<P_hª´ΩK‰˝<Ω«”õºA=øΩ§*ΩÛ”≈</M°<éÈ=u¥ª{"title": "PSA:Prostate-Specific Antigen (PSA) is a protein produced by prostate cells, commonly measured to assess prostate health. It serves as a crucial marker for evaluating prostate health, particularly in the context of testosterone therapy, where monitoring PSA levels can provide important insights into the condition of the prostate."}{"title": "MUTACIONES DEL GEN RSPO1:Mutations in the RSPO1 gene are associated with conditions like hyperkeratosis palmoplantar and squamous cell carcinoma, affecting sexual development."}{"title": "VARONES 46,XX:"}{"title": "ENFERMEDAD DE ADDISON:Addison's disease, known as \"enfermedad de Addison,\" is an autoimmune condition characterized by the insufficient production of hormones by the adrenal glands. This disorder can occur in patients who have other autoimmune disorders, such as type 1 diabetes mellitus. It is classified as an adrenal insufficiency and is one of the endocrine abnormalities that may manifest in autoimmune polyglandular syndromes. Management of Addison's disease often requires dietary adjustments, particularly in sodium and potassium intake, to help regulate the body's hormonal balance."}{"title": "GEN AIRE:El gen AIRE es un gen regulador autoinmune que, cuando presenta mutaciones, est\u00e1 asociado con el s\u00edndrome poliglandular autoinmune de tipo 1."}{"title": "CANDIDIASIS MUCOCUT\u00c1NEA:La candidiasis mucocut\u00e1nea es una infecci\u00f3n f\u00fangica que puede presentarse en la piel, u\u00f1as y mucosas, y es una manifestaci\u00f3n com\u00fan en el s\u00edndrome poliglandular autoinmune de tipo 1."}{"title": "DIABETES DE TIPO 1:La diabetes de tipo 1 es una enfermedad autoinmunitaria que puede asociarse con el s\u00edndrome poliglandular autoinmune de tipo 1."}{"title": "TIROIDITIS AUTOINMUNE CR\u00d3NICA:Chronic autoimmune thyroiditis, known as \"tiroiditis autoinmune cr\u00f3nica,\" is a condition that can manifest in patients with autoimmune polyendocrine syndrome, impacting thyroid function. Additionally, it is associated with adrenal insufficiency in individuals diagnosed with POEMS syndrome. This highlights the condition's relevance in the context of broader autoimmune disorders and its potential complications."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME POLIGLANDULAR AUTOINMUNE TIPO 1:The \"S\u00edndrome Poliglandular Autoinmune Tipo 1\" is a rare autoimmune disorder characterized by a combination of several autoimmune conditions. It includes mucocutaneous candidiasis, which affects the skin and mucous membranes, hypoparathyroidism, a condition where the parathyroid glands produce insufficient hormones, and Addison's disease, which is characterized by insufficient production of hormones by the adrenal glands. This syndrome may also involve other autoimmune disorders, highlighting its complex nature and the interplay of various immune system dysfunctions."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME POLIGLANDULAR AUTOINMUNE TIPO 2:The \"S\u00edndrome Poliglandular Autoinmune Tipo 2\" is a condition characterized by the presence of multiple autoimmune disorders. It includes Addison's disease, autoimmune thyroid disease, type 1 diabetes mellitus, and other autoimmune conditions. This syndrome is more prevalent than type 1 autoimmune polyglandular syndrome and is linked to genetic factors, particularly the HLA-DR3 allele."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME POLIGLANDULAR AUTOINMUNE TIPO 3:El s\u00edndrome poliglandular autoinmune tipo 3 es m\u00e1s heterog\u00e9neo y asocia endocrinopat\u00edas autoinmunes sin enfermedad de Addison, incluyendo tiroidopat\u00eda autoinmune y diabetes mellitus tipo 1."}{"title": "TIROIDITIS CR\u00d3NICA AUTOINMUNE:La tiroiditis cr\u00f3nica autoinmune es una enfermedad que afecta la tiroides y puede asociarse con otros trastornos autoinmunes."}{"title": "OOFORITIS AUTOINMUNE:OOFORITIS AUTOINMUNE, or autoimmune oophoritis, is a condition characterized by lymphocytic infiltration of ovarian follicles. This infiltration leads to primary ovarian insufficiency, which is a significant consequence of the disorder. Additionally, autoimmune oophoritis is associated with other autoimmune disorders, indicating a broader context of autoimmune activity in affected individuals."}{"title": "INSUFICIENCIA SUPRARRENAL AUTOINMUNITARIA:La insuficiencia suprarrenal autoinmunitaria es una condici\u00f3n en la que las gl\u00e1ndulas suprarrenales no producen suficientes hormonas, a menudo asociada con autoanticuerpos antiadrenales."}{"title": "VIT\u00cdLIGO:El vit\u00edligo es una enfermedad autoinmune que causa la p\u00e9rdida de pigmento en la piel y puede asociarse con otros trastornos autoinmunes."}{"title": "INSUFICIENCIA OV\u00c1RICA PRIMARIA:Primary ovarian insufficiency is defined by primary hypogonadism before the age of 40 in women and is associated with autoimmune conditions."}{"title": "AUTOANTICUERPOS:Autoantibodies are markers that can indicate autoimmune conditions, including those related to ovarian insufficiency and Addison's disease."}{"title": "ANTICUERPOS ANTIADRENALES:Anti-adrenal antibodies are markers that may indicate the risk of developing Addison's disease in patients with autoimmune conditions."}{"title": "ANTICUERPOS ANTI-21 HIDROXILASA:Anti-21 hydroxylase antibodies are associated with adrenal insufficiency and can precede the onset of Addison's disease."}{"title": "POEMS:POEMS is a rare paraneoplastic syndrome characterized by polyneuropathy, organomegaly, endocrinopathy, monoclonal plasma cell disorder, and skin changes."}{"title": "INSUFICIENCIA SUPRARENAL:Adrenal insufficiency, also known as \"insuficiencia suprarrenal,\" is a condition characterized by the inadequate production of hormones by the adrenal glands. This condition can arise in patients undergoing treatment with immune checkpoint inhibitors, necessitating careful management to address the hormonal deficiencies. Additionally, adrenal insufficiency is recognized as a less common endocrinopathy associated with POEMS syndrome, a rare disorder that affects multiple systems in the body. In patients with Adrenoleukodystrophy, the diagnosis of insuficiencia suprarrenal can be confirmed through MRI findings, highlighting the importance of imaging in the assessment of this condition. Overall, adrenal insufficiency presents a significant clinical challenge that requires thorough evaluation and management in various contexts."}{"title": "ALHAMBRA PRISON:Alhambra Prison is a facility that is referenced in the context of the treatment of patients with adrenal insufficiency. Additionally, it serves as a type of institution where patients with diabetes may receive treatment for related health issues. While the text does not explicitly detail its role in diabetes care, the mention of Alhambra Prison highlights its relevance in the broader context of healthcare for individuals with endocrine disorders."}{"title": "CTLA-4:CTLA-4 is a gene involved in immune regulation, referenced in relation to the genetic factors associated with SPA type 2."}{"title": "PTPN22:PTPN22 is a gene that plays a role in immune system regulation, mentioned in the context of genetic associations with SPA type 2."}{"title": "CLEC16A:CLEC16A is a gene associated with immune regulation, noted in the discussion of genetic factors related to SPA type 2."}{"title": "PTH:PTH, or parathyroid hormone, is a crucial hormone that regulates calcium and phosphorus levels in the body. It plays a significant role in maintaining calcium homeostasis by influencing the absorption and reabsorption of calcium, as well as decreasing the tubular reabsorption of phosphorus. PTH is particularly important in the context of vitamin D deficiency, as its levels may become elevated in such cases. Additionally, PTH is involved in the pathophysiology of hypocalcemia and is essential for bone metabolism. Overall, PTH is vital for ensuring proper calcium levels in the blood and supporting various physiological processes related to bone health."}{"title": "ANGIOTENSIN II:Angiotensin II is a hormone that increases blood pressure and stimulates the release of aldosterone."}{"title": "NATRIURETIC PEPTIDE:Atrial natriuretic peptide is a hormone that helps regulate blood pressure and fluid balance."}{"title": "NITRIC OXIDE:Nitric oxide is a signaling molecule that plays a role in various physiological processes, including vasodilation."}{"title": "PROGESTERONE:Progesterone is a hormone that plays a crucial role in preparing the uterus for pregnancy and regulating the menstrual cycle. Additionally, when administered cyclically, progesterone has been shown to increase bone mass in adolescents suffering from Anorexia Nervosa. This dual function highlights its importance not only in reproductive health but also in supporting bone density in vulnerable populations."}{"title": "THYROID HORMONES:"}{"title": "KIDNEYS:The kidneys are vital organs in the human body that play a crucial role in various physiological processes. In addition to their primary function of filtering blood and producing urine, the kidneys also participate in gluconeogenesis, although to a lesser extent than the liver. This metabolic process is essential for maintaining blood glucose levels, particularly during periods of fasting or intense exercise."}{"title": "RECEPTORES INTRACELULARES:Intracellular receptors are proteins that bind to lipophilic hormones and mediate their effects by regulating gene transcription."}{"title": "CICLOPENTANO-PERHIDROFENANTRENO:Ciclopentano-perhidrofenantreno is a chemical structure from which steroid hormones are derived, synthesized from cholesterol."}{"title": "SRE:Steroid Response Elements (SRE) are specific DNA sequences that steroid hormone-receptor complexes bind to, regulating gene transcription."}{"title": "5'-YODINASA:5'-iodinase is an enzyme that converts T4 to T3 in target cells, activating the thyroid hormone's effects."}{"title": "HORMONAS ESTEROIDEAS:Steroid hormones are lipid-derived hormones that regulate various physiological processes through intracellular receptors."}{"title": "HORMONAS LIPOF\u00cdLICAS:"}{"title": "PPAR:PPAR (Peroxisome Proliferator Activated Receptor) is a nuclear receptor that acts as a transcription factor in response to metabolic stimuli."}{"title": "FIBRATOS:Fibrates are a class of medications that target PPAR (peroxisome proliferator-activated receptor) receptors to regulate lipid levels in the body. They are primarily used to treat dyslipidemia, particularly in patients with metabolic disorders. Fibrates are effective in managing hypertriglyceridemia, functioning as agonists of the PPAR-\u03b1 receptor, which plays a crucial role in lipid metabolism. However, it is important to note that fibrates can have gastrointestinal side effects and are contraindicated in individuals with advanced liver and kidney disease."}{"title": "PLACENTA:The placenta is an organ that provides nutrients and oxygen to the fetus and secretes hormones during pregnancy."}{"title": "FETO:The fetus is the developing offspring in the womb that relies on the mother for nutrients and energy."}{"title": "RESISTENCIA A LA INSULINA:\"RESISTENCIA A LA INSULINA\" es una condici\u00f3n metab\u00f3lica que se caracteriza por una disminuci\u00f3n en la capacidad del cuerpo para utilizar la insulina de manera efectiva. Esta condici\u00f3n puede aumentar durante el embarazo, lo que afecta la captaci\u00f3n de glucosa y el metabolismo de la madre. Adem\u00e1s, la resistencia a la insulina tambi\u00e9n puede presentarse en pacientes cr\u00edticamente enfermos, impactando negativamente su metabolismo. Asimismo, se ha observado que este trastorno metab\u00f3lico puede ocurrir en pacientes con c\u00e1ncer, lo que repercute en su nutrici\u00f3n y salud general. En resumen, la resistencia a la insulina es un fen\u00f3meno que puede afectar a diferentes grupos de pacientes, incluyendo a mujeres embarazadas y aquellos con enfermedades graves, como el c\u00e1ncer."}{"title": "VOLUMEN PLASM\u00c1TICO:Cantidad de plasma en la sangre que aumenta significativamente durante el embarazo."}{"title": "CALCIURIA:Calciuria refers to the presence of calcium in the urine, a condition that can influence calcium availability for fetal development. It is characterized by the excretion of calcium in the urine, which tends to increase during pregnancy. This heightened excretion may have implications for both maternal and fetal health, particularly in ensuring adequate calcium levels for the developing fetus."}{"title": "HORMONAS DIABETOG\u00c9NICAS:"}{"title": "WOMEN'S HEALTH INITIATIVE:The Women's Health Initiative is a long-term national health study focused on addressing the most common causes of death, disability, and poor quality of life in postmenopausal women. This initiative investigates various health issues pertinent to this demographic, including the relationship between protein intake and frailty. Through its comprehensive approach, the Women's Health Initiative aims to enhance the understanding of health challenges faced by postmenopausal women and improve their overall well-being."}{"title": "HORMONE REPLACEMENT THERAPY:Hormone replacement therapy with estrogens is used in postmenopausal women to seek cardiovascular benefits but has associated risks."}{"title": "TESTOSTERONE THERAPY:Testosterone therapy is administered to men and requires evaluation of prostate size, PSA levels, and hematocrit before and during treatment."}{"title": "BASEDOW'S DISEASE:Basedow's disease is an autoimmune disorder that can cause hyperthyroidism and may lead to spontaneous remission after treatment."}{"title": "MULTINODULAR GOITER:Multinodular goiter is a condition that often requires early treatment with I-131 due to low incidence of hypothyroidism and low probability of spontaneous remission."}{"title": "CARDIAC DISEASE:Cardiac disease is a condition that may necessitate treatment for subclinical hyperthyroidism in older adults."}{"title": "FIBRILLATION AURICULAR:Atrial fibrillation is a potential complication associated with untreated subclinical hyperthyroidism in older adults."}{"title": "PREGNANCY:Pregnancy is a physiological condition characterized by various metabolic adaptations in the mother that are essential for supporting fetal development. It necessitates careful nutritional management, particularly for women with diabetes, to ensure both proper fetal growth and the health of the mother."}{"title": "HYPERTIROIDISMO SUBCL\u00cdNICO:Subclinical hyperthyroidism is a condition characterized by low TSH levels with normal FT4 levels, which may require treatment in certain populations."}{"title": "MENOPAUSIA:Menopause is a natural biological process marking the end of a woman's reproductive years, often associated with hormonal changes and health risks."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DEL T\u00daNEL CARPIANO:Carpal tunnel syndrome is a condition that may be associated with the use of growth hormone in older adults."}{"title": "HORMONAL RESISTANCE:Hormonal resistance is a condition where an organ does not respond adequately to a biologically active hormone, often due to genetic alterations affecting hormone receptors."}{"title": "CYTOCHROME CYP3A4:Cytochrome CYP3A4 is an enzyme that plays a crucial role in the metabolism of many drugs, affecting their efficacy and safety."}{"title": "YIALAMAS MA:Yialamas MA is a co-author of the clinical practice guideline on testosterone therapy in men with hypogonadism."}{"title": "BRITO JP:Brito JP is a contributor to the clinical practice guideline on testosterone therapy in men with hypogonadism."}{"title": "CUNNINGHAM GR:Cunningham GR is one of the authors of the clinical practice guideline on testosterone therapy in men with hypogonadism."}{"title": "HAYES FJ:Hayes FJ is a co-author of the clinical practice guideline on testosterone therapy in men with hypogonadism."}{"title": "HODIS HN:Hodis HN is one of the authors of the clinical practice guideline on testosterone therapy in men with hypogonadism."}{"title": "BAHN R:Bahn R is a contributor to the textbook on endocrinology, discussing hyperthyroid disorders."}{"title": "KOKSHOORN NE:Kokshoorn NE is an author of a systematic review on GH replacement therapy in elderly GH-deficient patients."}{"title": "BIERMASZ NR:Biermasz NR is a co-author of a systematic review on GH replacement therapy in elderly GH-deficient patients."}{"title": "ROELFSEMA F:Roelfsema F is a contributor to the systematic review on GH replacement therapy in elderly GH-deficient patients."}{"title": "SMIT JWA:Smit JWA is one of the authors of the systematic review on GH replacement therapy in elderly GH-deficient patients."}{"title": "PEREIRA AM:Pereira AM is a co-author of the systematic review on GH replacement therapy in elderly GH-deficient patients."}{"title": "ROMIJN JA:Romijn JA is a contributor to the systematic review on GH replacement therapy in elderly GH-deficient patients."}{"title": "BHASIN S:"}{"title": "GH REPLACEMENT THERAPY:"}{"title": "CYP450:CYP450 is a family of enzymes that catalyze oxidation reactions and are crucial for drug metabolism in humans."}{"title": "CYP3A4:CYP3A4 is the most important member of the CYP450 family, responsible for the metabolism of approximately half of the drugs used in human therapy."}{"title": "RIFAMPICINA:Rifampicina is an antibiotic that is primarily used to treat tuberculosis and other bacterial infections. In addition to its antimicrobial properties, Rifampicina can induce the enzyme CYP3A4, which plays a significant role in drug metabolism. This induction can affect the metabolism of various medications, potentially altering their effectiveness and safety profiles."}{"title": "ANTIF\u00daNGICOS:Antifungals are drugs that can inhibit the enzyme CYP3A4, necessitating dosage reductions of drugs metabolized by this enzyme."}{"title": "ANTIBI\u00d3TICOS MACR\u00d3LIDOS:Macrolide antibiotics are drugs that can inhibit CYP3A4, affecting the metabolism of other medications."}{"title": "NIVOLUMAB:Nivolumab is an immune checkpoint inhibitor that targets PD-1 and is used in treating various cancers."}{"title": "PEMBROLIZUMAB:Pembrolizumab is an immune checkpoint inhibitor that targets PD-1, used in the treatment of melanoma and other cancers."}{"title": "ATEZOLIZUMAB:Atezolizumab is an immune checkpoint inhibitor that targets PD-L1, used in treating several types of cancer."}{"title": "AVELUMAB:Avelumab is an immune checkpoint inhibitor that targets PD-L1, utilized in cancer therapy."}{"title": "DURVALUMAB:Durvalumab is an immune checkpoint inhibitor that targets PD-L1, used in the treatment of various malignancies."}{"title": "MELANOMA:Melanoma is a type of skin cancer that can be treated with immune checkpoint inhibitors such as ipilimumab and nivolumab. Additionally, it is noted that patients with Multiple Endocrine Neoplasia type 1 (MEN1) may develop melanoma; however, the specific connection between melanoma and the MEN1 gene has not been described."}{"title": "CARCINOMA DE C\u00c9LULAS RENALES:Renal cell carcinoma is a type of kidney cancer that can be treated with immune checkpoint inhibitors."}{"title": "C\u00c1NCER DE PULM\u00d3N DE C\u00c9LULAS NO PEQUE\u00d1AS:Non-small cell lung cancer is a type of lung cancer that can be treated with immune checkpoint inhibitors."}{"title": "HORMONAL ALTERATIONS:Hormonal alterations are changes in hormone levels that can occur as a result of immune checkpoint blockade."}{"title": "ENDOCRINOPAT\u00cdAS:Endocrinopathies are disorders related to the endocrine system that can arise from immune checkpoint inhibitors."}{"title": "CHECKPOINT:"}{"title": "EMA:The European Medicines Agency (EMA) is an agency of the European Union tasked with the evaluation, supervision, and safety monitoring of medicinal products. It plays a crucial role in ensuring the safety and efficacy of medicines available in the EU. The EMA has been involved in the review of various medicinal products, including obesity treatments such as lorcaserin, which it did not approve for marketing due to safety concerns. Additionally, the agency has rejected certain obesity treatments, including fentermina and topiramato, based on risk assessments. Overall, the EMA is dedicated to maintaining high standards for medicinal products within the European Union, focusing on the health and safety of the public."}{"title": "LYSODREN:Lysodren is a medication with the active ingredient mitotane, used in the treatment of adrenal cancer."}{"title": "YERVOY:Yervoy is a medication with the active ingredient ipilimumab, used in cancer immunotherapy."}{"title": "MITOTANE:Mitotane is a drug used to treat adrenal cancer by inhibiting adrenal cortex function."}{"title": "ZARZUELO A:Zarzuelo A is an author who contributed to the book on pharmacological interactions."}{"title": "FLUDROCORTISONA:Fludrocortisona, also known as fludrocortisone, is a synthetic corticosteroid medication primarily used in the treatment of isolated aldosterone deficiency and adrenal insufficiency. It plays a crucial role in managing conditions related to insufficient production of aldosterone, helping to regulate sodium and potassium levels in the body."}{"title": "HYPERURICEMIA:Hyperuricemia is a medical condition characterized by elevated levels of uric acid in the blood. This condition can lead to various health issues, most notably gout, and is often influenced by dietary factors, including purine intake and alcohol consumption. Hyperuricemia is relevant in the context of dietary management for conditions such as nephrolithiasis and can frequently occur in patients. It may also be a complication associated with Glycogen Storage Disease I (GSDI). Treatment for hyperuricemia typically involves dietary modifications and medical intervention to manage uric acid levels effectively."}{"title": "ALTERACI\u00d3N:Alterations refer to changes in normal physiological functions, often leading to medical conditions."}{"title": "INMUNIDAD:INMUNIDAD refers to the body's ability to resist infections and diseases through various biological mechanisms. This concept encompasses the various ways in which the immune system protects the body from harmful pathogens and maintains overall health."}{"title": "\u00c1CIDO \u00daRICO:\u00c1cido \u00farico is a waste product formed from the breakdown of purines, primarily produced in the liver and to a lesser extent in the small intestine. It serves as the final product of purine metabolism. While \u00e1cido \u00farico acts as a potent extracellular antioxidant, it can also induce oxidative stress in certain cells, which is associated with an increased risk of cardiovascular diseases. Elevated levels of \u00e1cido \u00farico can lead to hyperuricemia, a condition that may result in various health issues, including gout and the formation of uric acid stones in the kidneys. Therefore, maintaining balanced levels of \u00e1cido \u00farico is crucial for overall health."}{"title": "HIPERURICEMIA:Hiperuricemia is a medical condition characterized by elevated levels of uric acid in the blood. This condition is often associated with various metabolic and vascular issues, including obesity, hypertension, and metabolic syndrome. Hiperuricemia can lead to several health complications, such as the formation of uric acid stones, gout, and an increased risk of cardiovascular disease. Additionally, it may contribute to other health problems, including renal disease and arthritis, particularly gouty arthritis. Overall, hiperuricemia represents a significant health concern due to its association with multiple serious conditions."}{"title": "ARTRITIS GOTOSA:La artritis gotosa es una enfermedad inflamatoria que se produce por la acumulaci\u00f3n de cristales de urato en las articulaciones, a menudo asociada con niveles elevados de \u00e1cido \u00farico."}{"title": "UROLITIASIS:La urolitiasis es la formaci\u00f3n de c\u00e1lculos en el tracto urinario, que puede ser consecuencia de la hiperuricemia y la acumulaci\u00f3n de \u00e1cido \u00farico."}{"title": "ENFERMEDAD NEFR\u00d3PATA:"}{"title": "NURIA VALDES GALLEGO:Nuria Valdes Gallego is a specialist in Endocrinology and Nutrition, with a degree in Biochemistry and a doctorate in Medicine. She is the head of the Endocrinology and Nutrition Section at the University Hospital of Cabue\u00f1es in Gij\u00f3n and an associate professor at the University of Oviedo."}{"title": "HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO DE CABUE\u00d1ES:The University Hospital of Cabue\u00f1es in Gij\u00f3n is where Nuria Valdes Gallego works as the head of the Endocrinology and Nutrition Section."}{"title": "UNIVERSIDAD DE OVIEDO:The University of Oviedo is where Nuria Valdes Gallego serves as an associate professor in Endocrinology and Nutrition."}{"title": "SOCIEDAD ASTURIANA DE DIABETES, ENDOCRINOLOG\u00cdA, NUTRICI\u00d3N Y OBESIDAD:The Asturian Society of Diabetes, Endocrinology, Nutrition, and Obesity is where Nuria Valdes Gallego served as treasurer from 2014 to 2016."}{"title": "GRUPO DE TRABAJO SOBRE NEOPLASIA ENDOCRINA M\u00daLTIPLE:The Working Group on Multiple Endocrine Neoplasia is a group Nuria Valdes Gallego coordinated from 2011 to 2017."}{"title": "GETNE:GETNE is an organization that awarded Nuria Valdes Gallego a research grant in 2015."}{"title": "SAPROPTERINA:Sapropterina is a synthetic preparation of tetrahydrobiopterin (BH4) that is utilized in the treatment of mild phenylketonuria (PKU). It is often administered alongside dietary management to enhance the patient's ability to tolerate phenylalanine (Phe). As a commercial preparation, Sapropterina plays a crucial role in managing PKU by increasing the tolerance to this amino acid, thereby aiding in the overall treatment strategy for individuals affected by this condition."}{"title": "FDA:The FDA, or Food and Drug Administration, is the U.S. government agency responsible for regulating food, pharmaceuticals, and medical devices. It plays a crucial role in overseeing the safety and efficacy of various products, including clinical nutrition items and obesity treatments such as lorcaserin and the combination of phentermine and topiramate. Additionally, the FDA approved teduglutide for use in patients with intestinal failure in December 2012. The agency categorizes drugs and treatments based on their safety and efficacy, ensuring that medications, including those for conditions like osteoporosis, meet the necessary standards before they can be made available to the public."}{"title": "HYPERCALCEMIA:Hypercalcemia is a medical condition characterized by an abnormally high level of calcium in the blood. This condition is often associated with various underlying medical issues, including hyperparathyroidism, certain cancers such as lymphomas, and parathyroid tumors, particularly in cases of Multiple Endocrine Neoplasia type 1 (MEN1). Additionally, hypercalcemia can be linked to hypomagnesemia and familial hypocalciuric hypercalcemia. Overall, hypercalcemia can arise from a range of conditions, highlighting its complexity and the need for careful diagnosis and management."}{"title": "HYPERPARATHYROIDISM:Hyperparathyroidism is a medical condition characterized by an excess production of parathyroid hormone (PTH) by the parathyroid glands. This overproduction leads to elevated levels of calcium in the blood, which can result in various health complications. The condition is often associated with multiple endocrine neoplasia (MEN) syndromes, particularly MEN1 and MEN2A. Additionally, hyperparathyroidism can arise from prolonged elevated levels of phosphorus in the blood, especially in patients with chronic kidney disease. Overall, hyperparathyroidism is marked by its impact on calcium metabolism and its potential links to genetic syndromes."}{"title": "EL-HAJJ FULEIHAN:El-Hajj Fuleihan is a medical professional and researcher who has made significant contributions to the understanding and management of primary hyperparathyroidism. His work has enhanced the knowledge surrounding the diagnosis and treatment of this condition, highlighting his role in advancing medical research in this area."}{"title": "SILVERBERG:Silverberg is a distinguished medical expert and researcher recognized for his contributions to the field of endocrinology, particularly in the management of primary hyperparathyroidism and its associated complications. He has published significant works that enhance the understanding of this condition. Additionally, Silverberg is known for his research on hypercalcemia of malignancy, focusing on its mechanisms and implications. His expertise in these areas underscores his important role in advancing medical knowledge and treatment strategies related to calcium metabolism disorders."}{"title": "YIP:Yip is a medical professional involved in the preoperative localization for parathyroid surgery in patients with primary hyperparathyroidism."}{"title": "HIPERPARATIROIDISMO SECUNDARIO:Hiperparatiroidismo secundario es una condici\u00f3n que se presenta como respuesta a niveles bajos de calcio en el organismo, frecuentemente asociada con la insuficiencia renal. Esta afecci\u00f3n se caracteriza por una producci\u00f3n excesiva de hormona paratiroidea por parte de las gl\u00e1ndulas paratiroides, que ocurre como resultado de la hipocalcemia. Es com\u00fanmente observada en pacientes con enfermedad renal cr\u00f3nica, donde la incapacidad de los ri\u00f1ones para mantener niveles adecuados de calcio contribuye al desarrollo de esta condici\u00f3n."}{"title": "HORMONA PARATIROIDEA:Hormona paratiroidea (PTH) is a polypeptide hormone produced by the parathyroid glands that plays a crucial role in regulating calcium levels in the blood. It functions to increase serum calcium levels and is influenced by the use of glucocorticoids. PTH is essential for maintaining calcium homeostasis in the body, ensuring that calcium levels remain within a healthy range."}{"title": "C\u00c1NCER DE RI\u00d1\u00d3N:El c\u00e1ncer de ri\u00f1\u00f3n es otro tipo de c\u00e1ncer que puede estar asociado con hipercalcemia, a menudo a trav\u00e9s de mecanismos tumorales."}{"title": "C\u00c1NCER DE PULM\u00d3N:C\u00c1NCER DE PULM\u00d3N, o c\u00e1ncer de pulm\u00f3n, es una enfermedad que se ha relacionado con diversos factores diet\u00e9ticos y de salud. Se ha observado que el consumo elevado de carne roja incrementa el riesgo de desarrollar esta neoplasia, mientras que la ingesta de carne de aves de corral parece tener un efecto protector, disminuyendo dicho riesgo. Adem\u00e1s, el c\u00e1ncer de pulm\u00f3n puede causar hipercalcemia en pacientes, lo cual a menudo est\u00e1 relacionado con met\u00e1stasis.\n\nLa influencia de la dieta en el c\u00e1ncer de pulm\u00f3n tambi\u00e9n se extiende a los \u00e1cidos grasos omega-3, cuya ingesta podr\u00eda tener un impacto, especialmente en mujeres, aunque los resultados de los estudios no son estad\u00edsticamente significativos. Por otro lado, el consumo de frutas y verduras se ha asociado con una disminuci\u00f3n en el riesgo de incidencia de c\u00e1ncer de pulm\u00f3n, sugiriendo que una dieta rica en estos alimentos puede ser beneficiosa. Asimismo, se ha planteado que el consumo de soja podr\u00eda reducir el riesgo de c\u00e1ncer de pulm\u00f3n, aunque la evidencia al respecto es limitada.\n\nEn resumen, el c\u00e1ncer de pulm\u00f3n es una enfermedad compleja influenciada por h\u00e1bitos diet\u00e9ticos, donde el consumo de carne roja aumenta el riesgo, mientras que el consumo de aves de corral, frutas, verduras y posiblemente soja podr\u00eda ayudar a reducirlo."}{"title": "MIELOMA M\u00daLTIPLE:Mieloma m\u00faltiple es un tipo de c\u00e1ncer de la sangre que se caracteriza por la proliferaci\u00f3n anormal de c\u00e9lulas plasm\u00e1ticas en la m\u00e9dula \u00f3sea. Esta enfermedad puede provocar hipercalcemia, que es un aumento de los niveles de calcio en la sangre, debido a la destrucci\u00f3n \u00f3sea asociada con el mieloma. Adem\u00e1s, se ha observado una posible asociaci\u00f3n entre el mieloma m\u00faltiple y el consumo elevado de pescado. En general, el mieloma m\u00faltiple puede afectar los niveles de calcio en la sangre, lo que se relaciona con anormalidades en la concentraci\u00f3n de este mineral."}{"title": "HYPERCALCEMIA MALIGNA:"}{"title": "HYPERPARATHYROIDISM SECUNDARY:"}{"title": "HODGKIN'S LYMPHOMA:Hodgkin's lymphoma is a type of cancer that affects the lymphatic system and is associated with hypercalcemia due to tumor production of 1,25-dihydroxyvitamin D."}{"title": "NON-HODGKIN'S LYMPHOMA:Non-Hodgkin's lymphoma is a group of blood cancers that includes all types of lymphoma except Hodgkin's lymphoma, also linked to hypercalcemia in some cases."}{"title": "PARATHYROID HORMONE (PTH):Parathyroid hormone is a hormone produced by the parathyroid glands that regulates calcium levels in the blood and is involved in the pathophysiology of hypercalcemia."}{"title": "CARCINOMA:Carcinoma refers to a type of cancer that starts in the skin or in tissues that line or cover internal organs, which can lead to ectopic PTH secretion and hypercalcemia."}{"title": "PRIMARY HYPERPARATHYROIDISM:Primary hyperparathyroidism is a specific type of hyperparathyroidism that occurs due to an issue within the parathyroid glands themselves, often leading to elevated calcium levels in the blood."}{"title": "NEPHROCALCINOSIS:Nephrocalcinosis is a condition characterized by the deposition of calcium in the renal parenchyma, often associated with hypercalcemia and hyperparathyroidism."}{"title": "CREATININE CLEARANCE:Creatinine clearance is a measure of kidney function that can be affected by hyperparathyroidism, particularly when levels fall below 60 ml/min."}{"title": "PARATHYROIDECTOMY:Parathyroidectomy is a surgical procedure to remove one or more parathyroid glands, often indicated in cases of symptomatic hyperparathyroidism."}{"title": "WORKSHOP:The Fourth International Workshop refers to a conference focused on guidelines for the management of hyperparathyroidism, providing recommendations for treatment."}{"title": "HIPERCALCEMIA HIPOCALCI\u00daRICA FAMILIAR:Hipercalcemia hipocalci\u00farica familiar (HHF) es un trastorno hereditario autos\u00f3mico dominante que afecta la regulaci\u00f3n del calcio en el cuerpo, causado por mutaciones en el gen receptor sensor del calcio (CASR)."}{"title": "PARATIROIDECTOM\u00cdA:La paratiroidectom\u00eda es una intervenci\u00f3n quir\u00fargica que puede beneficiar a pacientes con hiperparatiroidismo primario leve y hipercalcemia hipocalci\u00farica familiar."}{"title": "CASR:El gen receptor sensor del calcio (CASR) es responsable de la regulaci\u00f3n del calcio en el cuerpo y su mutaci\u00f3n puede causar hipercalcemia hipocalci\u00farica familiar."}{"title": "PTHRP:PTHRP, or parathyroid hormone-related peptide, is a protein that plays a significant role in regulating calcium levels in the body. It is particularly noted for its association with malignancies, as it can lead to hypercalcemia, a condition characterized by elevated calcium levels in the blood. This effect is especially observed in patients with solid tumors that are not metastatic. PTHrP's ability to induce hypercalcemia highlights its importance in the context of certain cancers and underscores its relevance in medical discussions surrounding tumor-related calcium dysregulation."}{"title": "HYPERCALCEMIA RELACIONADA CON PTHRP:La hipercalcemia relacionada con PTHrP elevada es una condici\u00f3n que representa hasta el 80% de los pacientes con hipercalcemia de malignidad."}{"title": "HYPERCALCEMIA DE MALIGNIDAD:La hipercalcemia de malignidad es una condici\u00f3n m\u00e9dica que se presenta en pacientes con c\u00e1ncer, donde la hipercalcemia es causada por mecanismos relacionados con tumores."}{"title": "SPECT:SPECT, which stands for Single Photon Emission Computed Tomography, is a nuclear imaging technique that generates three-dimensional images of the body. This advanced imaging modality is often utilized in conjunction with other imaging techniques to enhance diagnostic accuracy. SPECT is particularly valuable in improving the detection of parathyroid glands, among other applications, making it a crucial tool in medical imaging."}{"title": "GAMMAGRAF\u00cdA CON SESTAMIBI:Gammagraf\u00eda con sestamibi is a type of imaging test used to locate parathyroid adenomas in patients suspected of having hyperparathyroidism."}{"title": "C\u00c1NCER ESOF\u00c1GICO:C\u00e1ncer esof\u00e1gico es una enfermedad maligna que afecta el es\u00f3fago, un \u00f3rgano crucial en el sistema digestivo. Esta condici\u00f3n puede tener efectos significativos sobre el estado nutricional de los pacientes, ya que puede llevar a complicaciones que afectan la ingesta y absorci\u00f3n de nutrientes. Adem\u00e1s, se ha observado que el c\u00e1ncer esof\u00e1gico puede estar asociado con la hipercalcemia, una condici\u00f3n caracterizada por niveles elevados de calcio en la sangre. Los estudios tambi\u00e9n indican que el consumo de carne roja y procesada est\u00e1 relacionado con un aumento en el riesgo de desarrollar carcinoma epidermoide, un tipo espec\u00edfico de c\u00e1ncer esof\u00e1gico. En resumen, el c\u00e1ncer esof\u00e1gico no solo representa un desaf\u00edo m\u00e9dico en t\u00e9rminos de tratamiento y manejo, sino que tambi\u00e9n plantea preocupaciones nutricionales significativas para quienes lo padecen."}{"title": "C\u00c1NCER DE CUELLO UTERINO BULBAR:C\u00e1ncer de cuello uterino bulbar is a type of cancer that can cause hypercalcemia."}{"title": "C\u00c1NCER RENAL:C\u00e1ncer renal is a type of kidney cancer that is often associated with hypercalcemia. It has been linked to obesity, which significantly increases the mortality risk for those affected. Research has also explored the relationship between c\u00e1ncer renal and dietary factors, particularly the consumption of fish and omega-3 fatty acids. Additionally, studies indicate that a diet rich in plant fiber and legumes may reduce the risk of developing this type of cancer."}{"title": "C\u00c1NCER VESICAL:C\u00e1ncer vesical, or bladder cancer, is a type of malignancy that can be influenced by various dietary factors. Research suggests that the antioxidant properties found in fruits and vegetables may play a role in reducing the risk of developing bladder cancer, particularly among smokers. Additionally, this type of cancer is associated with certain health complications, such as hypercalcemia. Furthermore, there is an increased risk of bladder cancer linked to the consumption of processed meats. Overall, dietary choices, particularly the intake of antioxidants from fruits and vegetables, are significant factors in the risk profile for c\u00e1ncer vesical."}{"title": "TUMORES DE C\u00c9LULAS DE LOS ISLOTES:Tumores de c\u00e9lulas de los islotes can also produce excess PTHrP, contributing to hypercalcemia."}{"title": "CARCINOIDES:Carcinoides are tumors that may lead to hypercalcemia through the production of PTHrP."}{"title": "LINFOMA DE LINFOCITOS T AGRESIVO:Linfoma de linfocitos T agresivo is a hematological cancer associated with excessive PTHrP production and hypercalcemia."}{"title": "C\u00c1NCER EPIDERMICO PULMONAR:"}{"title": "HPP:HPP refers to Hyperparathyroidism, a medical condition characterized by the overproduction of parathyroid hormone, which can lead to elevated levels of calcium in the blood. This condition necessitates careful diagnosis and management primarily based on biochemical findings rather than imaging studies. Additionally, hyperparathyroidism can be associated with Multiple Endocrine Neoplasia type 1 (MEN1), a genetic disorder that affects the endocrine glands."}{"title": "MIBI:MIBI refers to Methoxyisobutylisonitrile, a radiopharmaceutical used in imaging studies for localizing parathyroid adenomas."}{"title": "REED LARSEN P:Reed Larsen P is a prominent co-author and contributor to the Williams Textbook of Endocrinology, a comprehensive resource that delves into various aspects of endocrine physiology and pathology. His work focuses on providing valuable insights into endocrine disorders, their management, and specific conditions such as insulinoma and hypercalcemia. Additionally, Reed Larsen P is recognized for his contributions related to neuroendocrine tumors within the context of the textbook. Overall, his expertise and authorship play a significant role in enhancing the understanding of endocrinology through this essential medical reference."}{"title": "BISPHOSPHONATES:Bisphosphonates are a class of medications that play a crucial role in the management of bone health. They are primarily known for their ability to inhibit bone resorption, making them effective in treating conditions such as hypercalcemia that arises from osteoclastic activity. Additionally, bisphosphonates are beneficial in preventing bone loss and may be indicated for certain patients with Anorexia Nervosa, especially those who are at risk of developing osteoporosis. This dual functionality highlights their importance in both general bone health management and specific clinical scenarios."}{"title": "FUROSEMIDE:Furosemide is a loop diuretic that can be used to promote calcium excretion but may worsen volume depletion if not used carefully."}{"title": "SERUM PHYSIOLOGICAL:Serum physiological refers to saline solution used for rehydration in patients with hypercalcemia."}{"title": "HYPERPLASIA PARATIROIDEA:Hyperplasia paratiroidea refers to the enlargement of the parathyroid glands, which can lead to increased calcium levels in the blood."}{"title": "FARMACOS ANTIRRESORTIVOS:Antiresorptive drugs are medications used to prevent the loss of bone mass and are often used in conjunction with calcitonin for treating severe hypercalcemia."}{"title": "PAMIDRONATO:Pamidronate is a bisphosphonate medication used to treat high calcium levels in the blood, particularly in cases of malignancy-related hypercalcemia."}{"title": "FUROSEMIDA:Furosemida, also known as furosemide, is a diuretic medication primarily used to treat fluid build-up associated with conditions such as heart failure, liver scarring, and kidney disease. It is effective in managing fluid retention and high blood pressure, and it can also assist in the treatment of hypercalcemia and hyponatremia by promoting the elimination of excess water from the body. \n\nTo maximize its effectiveness, furosemida should be taken on an empty stomach, as food can alter gastrointestinal motility and reduce its bioavailability. Additionally, it is often used in conjunction with other treatments for conditions like the Syndrome of Inappropriate Antidiuretic Hormone secretion (SIADH). Overall, furosemida plays a crucial role in managing fluid balance and sodium levels in patients with various medical conditions."}{"title": "SUERO SALINO:Saline solution is often used in medical treatments to help hydrate patients and can be part of the management strategy for hypercalcemia."}{"title": "SHANE E:Shane E is an author referenced in the context of hypercalcemia treatment in UpToDate."}{"title": "BERENSON JR:Berenson JR is an author referenced in the context of hypercalcemia treatment in UpToDate."}{"title": "EASTELL R:Eastell R is an author of clinical practice guidelines focused on the pharmacological management of osteoporosis in postmenopausal women."}{"title": "GOLTZMAN D:Goltzman D is an author recognized for his contributions to the understanding of hypocalcemia, particularly focusing on its diagnostic approaches and etiology in adults. His work emphasizes the importance of accurately diagnosing hypocalcemia and exploring its underlying causes, providing valuable insights into this medical condition."}{"title": "PSEUDOHYPOPARATHYROIDISM:Pseudohypoparathyroidism is a condition characterized by resistance to parathyroid hormone (PTH) action, leading to hypocalcemia and hyperphosphatemia."}{"title": "DISECCI\u00d3N CERVICAL:Disecci\u00f3n cervical is a surgical procedure that involves the removal of lymph nodes in the neck, often performed in cancer treatment, which can impact parathyroid function."}{"title": "OSTEODISTROFIA HEREDITARIA DE ALBRIGHT:Osteodistrofia hereditaria de Albright is a genetic disorder characterized by bone abnormalities and resistance to parathyroid hormone."}{"title": "GNAS1:GNAS1 is a gene that encodes the alpha subunit of the G protein that binds to the PTH/PTHrP receptor, playing a crucial role in signal transduction for parathyroid hormone responses."}{"title": "OSTEODYSTROFIA HEREDITARIA DE ALBRIGHT:Osteodystrophy is a condition characterized by round faces, short stature, short fourth metacarpal bones, obesity, subcutaneous calcifications, and developmental delay, associated with mutations in GNAS1."}{"title": "PSEUDOPSEUDOHIPOPARATIROIDISMO:Pseudopseudohypoparathyroidism is a condition where individuals have the phenotype of osteodystrophy but normal serum calcium, phosphate, and PTH levels due to the normal maternal allele."}{"title": "PSEUDOHIPOPARATIROIDISMO TIPO 1A:Type 1a pseudohypoparathyroidism is an autosomal dominant condition requiring maternal transmission of the mutation, leading to resistance to hormones coupled with G proteins."}{"title": "PSEUDOHIPOPARATIROIDISMO TIPO 1B:Type 1b pseudohypoparathyroidism is characterized by hypocalcemia without the phenotypic anomalies of osteodystrophy, with resistance to PTH confined to the kidney."}{"title": "PSEUDOHIPOPARATIROIDISMO TIPO 1C:Type 1c pseudohypoparathyroidism involves mutations affecting G protein coupling to the PTH/PTHrP receptor, leading to resistance to other hormones while maintaining the ability to stimulate adenyl cyclase."}{"title": "PSEUDOHIPOPARATIROIDISMO TIPO 2:Type 2 pseudohypoparathyroidism shows normal AMPc response to PTH but abnormal phosphaturia, lacking the osteodystrophy phenotype and familial characteristics."}{"title": "DIAG\u00c9ORGE:DiGeorge syndrome is a genetic disorder that can lead to various health issues, including hypoparathyroidism and calcium metabolism disorders."}{"title": "HORMONA PARATIROIDEA (PTH):Parathyroid hormone (PTH) is a hormone produced by the parathyroid glands that regulates calcium levels in the blood and bone metabolism."}{"title": "HORMONA LUTEINIZANTE:La hormona luteinizante, conocida como LH (luteinizing hormone en ingl\u00e9s), es una hormona producida por la gl\u00e1ndula pituitaria. Esta hormona desempe\u00f1a un papel crucial en la regulaci\u00f3n del ciclo menstrual y la ovulaci\u00f3n, siendo fundamental para el funcionamiento del sistema reproductivo."}{"title": "HORMONA ESTIMULANTE DEL FOL\u00cdCULO:Follicle-stimulating hormone (FSH) is a hormone involved in the regulation of reproductive processes, including the development of eggs in ovaries and sperm in testes."}{"title": "HORMONA LIBERADORA DE GONADOTROPINA (GNRH):Gonadotropin-releasing hormone (GnRH) is a hormone responsible for the release of FSH and LH from the pituitary gland, playing a crucial role in reproductive health."}{"title": "RECEPTOR PTH/PTHRP:The PTH/PTHrP receptor is a receptor that binds parathyroid hormone and parathyroid hormone-related peptide, mediating their effects on calcium and phosphate metabolism."}{"title": "ADENIL-CICLASA:Adenyl cyclase is an enzyme that converts ATP to cyclic AMP, playing a key role in signal transduction pathways, including those activated by hormones like PTH."}{"title": "HORMONAS ACOPLADAS A PROTE\u00cdNA G:G protein-coupled hormones are a class of hormones that exert their effects through G protein-coupled receptors, influencing various physiological processes."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DE DIGEORGE:El s\u00edndrome de DiGeorge es un trastorno cong\u00e9nito que se asocia con la ausencia de gl\u00e1ndulas paratiroides y otras anomal\u00edas cong\u00e9nitas."}{"title": "ALCALINAS:Las fosfatasas alcalinas son enzimas que pueden elevarse en la deficiencia de vitamina D, indicando problemas en el metabolismo \u00f3seo."}{"title": "RAQUITISMO:RAQUITISMO, tambi\u00e9n conocido como raquitismo, es una enfermedad metab\u00f3lica \u00f3sea que afecta principalmente a los ni\u00f1os y resulta de la deficiencia de vitamina D. Esta condici\u00f3n se caracteriza por un desarrollo \u00f3seo inadecuado, lo que provoca la desmineralizaci\u00f3n en la placa de crecimiento y, como consecuencia, deformidades \u00f3seas. Adem\u00e1s, el raquitismo puede desarrollarse en pacientes cel\u00edacos debido a la malabsorci\u00f3n de calcio y vitamina D, y tambi\u00e9n puede ser una complicaci\u00f3n de la enfermedad de Wilson. En resumen, el raquitismo es una enfermedad que lleva a la formaci\u00f3n de huesos blandos y d\u00e9biles, afectando gravemente el crecimiento y desarrollo de los ni\u00f1os."}{"title": "FOSFATASA ALCALINA:Alkaline phosphatase is an enzyme that is often elevated in cases of bone disease and is used as a marker in diagnosing conditions related to bone metabolism."}{"title": "25(OH)D:25-hydroxyvitamin D is a form of vitamin D that is measured in the blood to assess vitamin D status."}{"title": "1,25(OH)\u2082D\u2083:1,25-dihydroxyvitamin D3 is the active form of vitamin D that regulates calcium and phosphate metabolism in the body."}{"title": "HIDROXILACI\u00d3N:Hydroxylation is a biochemical process that activates vitamin D in the liver and kidneys."}{"title": "DAWSON-HUGHES B.:Dawson-Hughes B. is an author who has contributed to the understanding of vitamin D deficiency in adults, focusing on its definition, clinical manifestations, and treatment."}{"title": "DREZNER MK.:Drezner MK. is an author who has explored the causes of vitamin D deficiency and resistance, contributing to the medical literature on the subject."}{"title": "ERGOCALCIFEROL:Ergocalciferol, also known as vitamin D2, is a form of vitamin D that is utilized to treat vitamin D deficiency and associated conditions. It plays a crucial role in maintaining healthy levels of vitamin D in the body, which is essential for various physiological functions."}{"title": "CALCIFEDIOL:Calcifediol is a metabolite of vitamin D that is used in the treatment of vitamin D deficiency."}{"title": "HYPOCALCEMIA:Hypocalcemia is a medical condition characterized by low levels of calcium in the blood. This condition can arise from various factors, including vitamin D deficiency. Additionally, hypocalcemia is commonly observed in a significant percentage of patients suffering from pancreatitis, where it is often associated with metabolic disturbances."}{"title": "HYPOPARATHYROIDISM:Hypoparathyroidism is a medical condition characterized by insufficient production of parathyroid hormone by the parathyroid glands. This deficiency results in low levels of calcium in the blood, which can lead to various complications, including potential bone issues. Patients with hypoparathyroidism often require treatment with vitamin D to help manage their calcium levels effectively."}{"title": "RADIATION ULTRAVIOLETA:Ultraviolet radiation is a type of light that helps the skin synthesize vitamin D when exposed, playing a crucial role in preventing vitamin D deficiency."}{"title": "MALABSORPTION:Malabsorption is a medical condition characterized by the intestine's inability to properly absorb nutrients from the gastrointestinal tract. This condition is often observed in patients with celiac disease and can result in various nutritional deficiencies, including vitamin D deficiency."}{"title": "ANTIEPILEPTIC MEDICATION:Antiepileptic medications can affect the metabolism of vitamin D, potentially leading to deficiencies in patients taking these drugs."}{"title": "TUBERCULOSTATIC MEDICATION:Tuberculostatic medications are used to treat tuberculosis and can also impact vitamin D metabolism, contributing to deficiency."}{"title": "DIHIDROTAQUISTEROL:Dihidrotaquisterol is a metabolite of vitamin D that can be used in specific medical conditions related to vitamin D metabolism."}{"title": "CALCIDIOL:Calcidiol is a vitamin D metabolite that does not require hepatic 25-hydroxylation and is useful in patients with liver disease."}{"title": "TALASEMIA:Thalassemia is a blood disorder that can lead to complications requiring multiple blood transfusions, potentially affecting parathyroid function."}{"title": "ASOCIACI\u00d3N AMERICANA DE REUMATOLOG\u00cdA:The American Rheumatology Association suggests guidelines for patients taking glucocorticoids to maintain calcium and vitamin D intake."}{"title": "ALENDRONATO:Alendronato, also known as Alendronate, is a bisphosphonate medication primarily used to treat osteoporosis. It is effective in reducing bone resorption and increasing bone mineral density, which helps to lower the risk of fractures in individuals with this condition."}{"title": "RISEDRONATO:Risedronate is a bisphosphonate medication that helps reduce the risk of vertebral and hip fractures in osteoporosis patients."}{"title": "IBANDRONATO:Ibandronate is a bisphosphonate that suppresses bone resorption and significantly reduces the rate of vertebral fractures."}{"title": "FRATURAS:Fractures are breaks in bones that can occur more frequently in individuals with osteoporosis, especially when treated with glucocorticoids."}{"title": "DREZNER MK:Drezner MK is a prominent figure in the field of medicine, particularly known for his contributions to clinical studies on osteoporosis, with a specific focus on diagnosis and evaluation in postmenopausal women. In addition to his research work, Drezner MK serves as an editor for UpToDate, a reputable resource that provides comprehensive medical information, including topics related to endocrine neoplasia. His dual roles in research and editorial work highlight his commitment to advancing medical knowledge and improving patient care in these important areas."}{"title": "ROSE HN:"}{"title": "RIZEDRONATO:Risedronato is a bisphosphonate medication that helps in the treatment of osteoporosis by reducing bone resorption and increasing bone mineral density."}{"title": "DENOSUMAB:Denosumab is a fully human monoclonal antibody that functions by inhibiting RANKL, a key factor in the regulation of bone resorption. This mechanism leads to a reduction in bone resorption and an increase in bone mineral density, making it an effective treatment for osteoporosis. Additionally, Denosumab has been utilized in patients suffering from chronic anorexia nervosa who also have osteoporosis, highlighting its versatility in addressing bone health in various clinical contexts."}{"title": "RALOXIFENO:Raloxifene is a selective estrogen receptor modulator that reduces the risk of vertebral and hip fractures in postmenopausal women with osteoporosis."}{"title": "ROSEN CJ:Rosen CJ is a prominent figure in the field of osteoporosis management, recognized for his contributions to clinical guidelines and research. He has authored several studies that enhance the understanding and treatment of osteoporosis. Additionally, Rosen CJ serves as an editor and contributor to UpToDate, where he focuses on the clinical features and evaluation of glucocorticoid-induced osteoporosis, further solidifying his expertise and influence in this area of medicine."}{"title": "BLACK DM:Black DM is a researcher actively engaged in the field of osteoporosis, focusing on studies and the development of clinical guidelines for its management. In addition to this work, Black DM is also investigating intestinal calcium absorption, particularly in the context of gastric bypass surgery. This dual focus highlights Black DM's commitment to advancing knowledge in both osteoporosis and the nutritional implications of surgical weight loss procedures."}{"title": "OSTEOCLASTO:Osteoclasts are cells that break down bone tissue, and their activity is inhibited by treatments like denosumab and bisphosphonates."}{"title": "RANELATO DE ESTRONCIO:Ranelato de estroncio, also known as strontium ranelate, is a medication specifically designed for the treatment of osteoporosis, particularly in postmenopausal women. It functions through a dual mechanism: it stimulates the absorption of calcium in the bones while simultaneously inhibiting the resorption of bone tissue. This unique action helps to reduce the risk of fractures and supports overall bone health in individuals suffering from osteoporosis."}{"title": "TAMOXIFENO:Tamoxifen, also known as Tamoxifeno, is a selective estrogen receptor modulator (SERM) that is primarily used in the treatment and prevention of breast cancer. In addition to its role in oncology, Tamoxifen has been noted for its effects on bone density, making it a multifaceted medication in the management of breast cancer and related health concerns."}{"title": "BISFOSFONATOS:BISFOSFONATOS are medications used as an adjunct treatment for patients with celiac disease to prevent the loss of bone mineral density."}{"title": "OSTEOCLASTOS:Osteoclasts are cells that break down bone tissue, playing a crucial role in bone remodeling and the pathophysiology of osteoporosis."}{"title": "HUESO TRABECULAR:Trabecular bone is the spongy tissue inside bones that is most affected by osteoporosis, particularly in postmenopausal women."}{"title": "DMO VERTEBRAL:DMO vertebral refers to vertebral bone mineral density, which is a crucial indicator of bone health and plays a significant role in assessing bone loss, particularly in cases of glucocorticoid-induced osteoporosis. It is sensitive to changes in osteoporosis, making it an important measure for monitoring bone density and overall skeletal health."}{"title": "GLUCOCORTICOID-INDUCED OSTEOPOROSIS:Glucocorticoid-induced osteoporosis is a medical condition resulting from the use of glucocorticoids, leading to bone density loss and increased fracture risk."}{"title": "OSTEOMALACIA ONCOG\u00c9NICA:La osteomalacia oncog\u00e9nica es un s\u00edndrome paraneopl\u00e1sico adquirido poco frecuente que se caracteriza por anomal\u00edas bioqu\u00edmicas y de mineralizaci\u00f3n \u00f3sea similares a las del raquitismo hipofosfat\u00e9mico."}{"title": "FGF23:El factor de crecimiento de fibroblastos 23 (FGF23) es una prote\u00edna fosfat\u00farica que se expresa y secreta ect\u00f3picamente en tumores mesenquimatosos asociados con la osteomalacia oncog\u00e9nica. Adem\u00e1s, FGF23 act\u00faa como un nuevo regulador del metabolismo fosfoc\u00e1lcico, influyendo en la eliminaci\u00f3n urinaria de f\u00f3sforo. Esta prote\u00edna desempe\u00f1a un papel crucial en la regulaci\u00f3n de los niveles de f\u00f3sforo en el organismo, lo que la convierte en un elemento importante en el estudio de trastornos relacionados con el metabolismo mineral."}{"title": "TUMORES MESENQUIMATOSOS:Los tumores mesenquimatosos son neoplasias polimorfas peque\u00f1as de crecimiento lento que pueden causar osteomalacia oncog\u00e9nica al secretar FGF23 y otras prote\u00ednas fosfat\u00faricas."}{"title": "HUESOS LARGOS:Los huesos largos son una de las localizaciones donde se pueden encontrar tumores mesenquimatosos que causan osteomalacia oncog\u00e9nica."}{"title": "EXTREMIDADES DISTALES:Las extremidades distales son otra localizaci\u00f3n donde se pueden encontrar tumores mesenquimatosos que causan osteomalacia oncog\u00e9nica."}{"title": "NASOFARINGE:La nasofaringe es una de las \u00e1reas anat\u00f3micas donde pueden localizarse tumores mesenquimatosos responsables de la osteomalacia oncog\u00e9nica."}{"title": "SENOS NASALES:Los senos nasales son otra localizaci\u00f3n donde se pueden encontrar tumores mesenquimatosos que causan osteomalacia oncog\u00e9nica."}{"title": "INGLE:La ingle es una de las \u00e1reas donde se pueden localizar tumores mesenquimatosos que causan osteomalacia oncog\u00e9nica."}{"title": "1\u0391-HIDROXILASA:1\u03b1-hidroxilasa is an enzyme crucial for the activation of vitamin D, affecting calcium and phosphate metabolism"}{"title": "CYP27B1:CYP27B1 is a gene that encodes the enzyme 1\u03b1-hidroxilasa, mutations of which can lead to vitamin D deficiency disorders"}{"title": "S\u00cdNTOMAS NEUROGLUCOP\u00c9NICOS:S\u00edntomas neuroglucop\u00e9nicos are symptoms resulting from low glucose levels affecting the brain, often seen in patients with insulinoma"}{"title": "S\u00cdNTOMAS SIMP\u00c1TICOS ADRENALES:S\u00edntomas simp\u00e1ticos adrenales are autonomic symptoms that can occur during hypoglycemic episodes"}{"title": "TUMORES ENDOCRINOS:Tumores endocrinos are tumors that arise from endocrine glands, including insulinomas"}{"title": "INSULINOMA:Insulinoma is a type of tumor that leads to hyperinsulinism, a condition characterized by excessive levels of insulin in the blood. This often results in hypoglycemia, which is a dangerously low level of glucose in the bloodstream. The diagnosis of insulinoma typically involves specific biochemical tests that help identify the presence of the tumor and assess its impact on insulin production."}{"title": "CRYER PE:Cryer PE is one of the authors of the guidelines for the evaluation and management of adult hypoglycemic disorders, contributing to the understanding of insulinoma."}{"title": "AXELROD L:Axelrod L is a co-author of the guidelines for the evaluation and management of adult hypoglycemic disorders, providing insights into insulinoma diagnosis."}{"title": "GROSSMAN AB:Grossman AB is a contributor to the clinical practice guidelines for managing hypoglycemic disorders, including insulinoma."}{"title": "PANCREAS:The pancreas is a vital organ in the body that plays a crucial role in glucose metabolism and hormone production. It is involved in the secretion of important hormones, including insulin, and is a site where various tumors, such as insulinomas and somatostatinomas, can develop. Additionally, the pancreas is the focus of research published in the journal \"Pancreas,\" which covers studies related to pancreatic diseases, including investigations into nutrition in acute pancreatitis."}{"title": "IGF-2:IGF-2 is a growth factor that can be overproduced in certain tumors, leading to hypoglycemia."}{"title": "CARCINOID SYNDROME:Carcinoid syndrome is a condition that occurs when vasoactive substances escape hepatic degradation, often associated with neuroendocrine tumors."}{"title": "FIBROSARCOMA:Fibrosarcoma is a type of mesenchymal tumor that can be associated with hypoglycemia due to the overproduction of IGF-2."}{"title": "HEMANGIOPERICITOMA:Hemangiopericytoma is a vascular tumor that can also lead to hypoglycemia through similar mechanisms as other tumors producing IGF-2."}{"title": "HEPATOCARCINOMA:Hepatocarcinoma is a type of liver cancer characterized by its association with various factors, including dietary influences, particularly the consumption of vegetables. It is noted to occur in less than 10% of patients with Glycogen Storage Disease Type III (GSDIII), making it a relatively rare complication in this population. Hepatocarcinoma is recognized as the most common epithelial tumor that can lead to hypoglycemia, primarily due to the overproduction of Insulin-like Growth Factor 2 (IGF-2). Additionally, hepatocellular carcinoma, which is another form of liver cancer, can also manifest in patients with GSDIII, although it is considered rare."}{"title": "GROWTH HORMONE (GH):Growth hormone is a hormone that can be suppressed in cases of hypoglycemia, affecting glucose metabolism."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME CARCINOIDE:El s\u00edndrome carcinoide es una condici\u00f3n m\u00e9dica caracterizada por rubefacci\u00f3n, diarrea, y otros s\u00edntomas debido a la liberaci\u00f3n de sustancias vasoactivas en la circulaci\u00f3n sist\u00e9mica."}{"title": "TRIPT\u00d3FANO:Tript\u00f3fano is an essential amino acid that plays a crucial role in various bodily functions, including the production of serotonin, a neurotransmitter that regulates mood, sleep, and appetite. In the body, tript\u00f3fano is converted into serotonin, highlighting its importance in maintaining mental health and overall well-being. However, the metabolism of tript\u00f3fano can be disrupted in patients with carcinoid syndrome, a condition that affects the body's ability to process this amino acid effectively. This alteration in metabolism can have significant implications for individuals suffering from this syndrome, emphasizing the need for understanding the role of tript\u00f3fano in both health and disease."}{"title": "SEROTONINA:Serotonina, or serotonin, is a neurotransmitter that plays a crucial role in various bodily functions. It is produced from the amino acid tryptophan and is primarily known for its involvement in regulating mood, intestinal permeability, weight control, and satiety. Additionally, serotonin has vasoconstrictive properties and is secreted by carcinoid tumors, which are a type of neuroendocrine tumor. In the liver, serotonin is metabolized to form 5-hydroxyindoleacetic acid (5-HIA). Furthermore, serotonin is mentioned in relation to the effects of tesofensina, a drug associated with weight loss. Overall, serotonin is a multifaceted substance that influences both psychological and physiological processes in the body."}{"title": "TNE PANCRE\u00c1TICOS:Los tumores neuroendocrinos pancre\u00e1ticos son un tipo de tumor que afecta al p\u00e1ncreas y se clasifican seg\u00fan el \u00edndice Ki-67 y otros factores."}{"title": "ECOCARDIOGRAF\u00cdA:ECOCARDIOGRAF\u00cdA es un procedimiento diagn\u00f3stico m\u00e9dico que utiliza ultrasonido para evaluar tanto la estructura como la funci\u00f3n del coraz\u00f3n. Este m\u00e9todo es especialmente \u00fatil para detectar lesiones en pacientes que presentan s\u00edndrome carcinoide, lo que resalta su importancia en la identificaci\u00f3n de condiciones card\u00edacas espec\u00edficas."}{"title": "CARCINOMAS:Los carcinomas son un tipo de c\u00e1ncer que puede incluir componentes no neuroendocrinos y se relacionan con los tumores neuroendocrinos."}{"title": "MASA TUMORAL:La masa tumoral se refiere al tama\u00f1o y extensi\u00f3n del tumor, que influye en la aparici\u00f3n del s\u00edndrome carcinoide."}{"title": "D\u00c9FICIT DE NIACINA:El d\u00e9ficit de niacina es una condici\u00f3n que puede causar s\u00edntomas como lesiones cut\u00e1neas, relacionados con el s\u00edndrome carcinoide."}{"title": "TUMORES CARCINOIDES:TUMORES CARCINOIDES are tumors that can be diagnosed through the measurement of 5-Hydroxyindoleacetic acid (5-HIA). These tumors are derived from enterchromaffin cells, which are specialized cells found in the gastrointestinal tract that produce serotonin."}{"title": "WHO CLASSIFICATION OF TUMOURS OF ENDOCRINE ORGANS:The WHO Classification of Tumours of Endocrine Organs is a publication that provides guidelines and classifications for endocrine tumors, including neuroendocrine tumors, as of the 4th edition published in 2017."}{"title": "GASTRINOMA:Gastrinomas are neuroendocrine tumors that secrete gastrin, often associated with the condition MEN1, and typically found in the duodenum."}{"title": "VIPOMA:VIPOMA is a syndrome and a type of pancreatic neuroendocrine tumor characterized by the secretion of vasoactive intestinal peptide (VIP). This condition leads to severe, intermittent watery diarrhea, hypokalemia (low potassium levels), and achlorhydria (absence of hydrochloric acid in gastric secretions). VIPomas are specifically neuroendocrine tumors that primarily originate in the pancreas and are known for causing chronic diarrhea due to the excessive release of VIP."}{"title": "GLUCAGONOMA:Glucagonomas are rare neuroendocrine tumors that secrete glucagon, leading to a specific syndrome characterized by weight loss and diabetes."}{"title": "SOMATOSTATINOMA:Somatostatinomas are very rare neuroendocrine tumors that secrete somatostatin, often found in the pancreas and duodenum."}{"title": "KLINSTRA DS:Klimstra DS is a researcher known for contributions to the pathology and classification of neuroendocrine neoplasms in the digestive system."}{"title": "PANCREATIC NEUROENDOCRINE TUMORS:Pancreatic neuroendocrine tumors are a specific type of neuroendocrine tumor that occurs in the pancreas, which can be functional or non-functional and vary in their clinical behavior."}{"title": "ADENOCARCINOMA:Adenocarcinoma is a type of cancer that forms in mucus-secreting glands and can be a component of neuroendocrine tumors, particularly in mixed neoplasms."}{"title": "CARCINOMA DE C\u00c9LULAS EN ANILLO DE SELLO:Ring cell carcinoma is a rare type of cancer characterized by ring-shaped cells and can be associated with neuroendocrine tumors."}{"title": "C\u00c1NCER DE C\u00c9LULAS ESCAMOSAS:Squamous cell carcinoma is a type of cancer that arises from squamous cells and can also be a component of mixed neuroendocrine neoplasms."}{"title": "\u00cdNDICE DE PROLIFERACI\u00d3N KI-67:The Ki-67 proliferation index is a marker used to determine the growth fraction of a given cell population, particularly in the context of neuroendocrine tumors."}{"title": "\u00cdNDICE MIT\u00d3TICO:The mitotic index is a measure of the number of cells undergoing mitosis in a given population, which is important for assessing the aggressiveness of tumors, including neuroendocrine tumors."}{"title": "NEUROENDOCRINE TUMORS:"}{"title": "SOMATOSTATINOMAS:Somatostatinomas are rare tumors that occur in the pancreas and duodenum, often associated with various syndromes and conditions."}{"title": "DUODENUM:The duodenum is the first part of the small intestine where somatostatinomas can also occur."}{"title": "NEUROFIBROMATOSIS TYPE 1:Neurofibromatosis type 1 is a genetic disorder that can be associated with duodenal tumors."}{"title": "VON HIPPEL-LINDAU SYNDROME:Von Hippel-Lindau syndrome is a genetic condition that can be associated with duodenal tumors."}{"title": "MEN1 SYNDROME:MEN1 syndrome is a hereditary condition that can lead to the development of pancreatic neuroendocrine tumors."}{"title": "CROMOGRANINS:Cromogranins are substances secreted by neuroendocrine tumors, often used as tumor markers."}{"title": "ENOLASA NEUROESPEC\u00cdFICA:Enolase neuroespec\u00edfica is another marker associated with neuroendocrine tumors."}{"title": "POLIP\u00c9PTIDO PANCRE\u00c1TICO:Pancreatic polypeptide is a hormone secreted by pancreatic neuroendocrine tumors."}{"title": "GHRELINA:Ghrelin, also known as \"GHRELINA,\" is a hormone primarily released in the gastric fundus. It is recognized as a potent orexigenic hormone, meaning it stimulates appetite by activating neuropeptide Y pathways in the brain. Additionally, ghrelin can be secreted by neuroendocrine tumors, which can further influence appetite and metabolism. This dual role highlights its significance in both normal physiological processes and potential pathological conditions."}{"title": "ERITEMA NECROL\u00cdTICO MIGRATORIO:Eritema necrol\u00edtico migratorio is a skin condition that can be associated with somatostatinomas and other neuroendocrine tumors."}{"title": "DIARREA CR\u00d3NICA:Chronic diarrhea, known as \"diarrea cr\u00f3nica,\" is a medical condition characterized by the persistent presence of diarrhea over an extended period. This condition is often associated with dehydration and malnutrition. It can manifest in infants, particularly when lactose is introduced, as seen in cases of glucose-galactose malabsorption. Additionally, chronic diarrhea can arise from various underlying conditions, including VIPoma, which is a type of neuroendocrine tumor. The prolonged nature of chronic diarrhea can lead to malabsorption issues, potentially resulting in complications such as hypophosphatemia."}{"title": "PANCREATECTOM\u00cdA DISTAL:Distal pancreatectomy is a surgical procedure aimed at treating tumors located in the tail of the pancreas. This operation involves the removal of a portion of the pancreas and is often performed alongside duodenotomy, particularly in cases involving gastrinomas."}{"title": "CARCINOMAS NEUROENDOCRINOS:Neuroendocrine carcinomas are poorly differentiated tumors that often have a high proliferation index and can metastasize quickly."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DE MEN1:MEN1 syndrome is a hereditary condition that predisposes individuals to multiple endocrine tumors, including pancreatic neuroendocrine tumors."}{"title": "NEUROFIBROMATOSIS:Neurofibromatosis is a genetic disorder that can be associated with the development of neuroendocrine tumors, particularly in the duodenum."}{"title": "TUMORES DE LAS C\u00c9LULAS DE LOS ISLOTES:Tumors of the islet cells are a type of neuroendocrine tumor that arises in the pancreas and can secrete hormones like insulin and glucagon.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "FEOCHROMOCITOMA:Pheochromocytoma is a tumor of the adrenal gland that is more frequent in patients with specific mutations in the RET proto-oncogene."}{"title": "HIGADO:Higado, commonly known as the liver, is a vital organ that plays a crucial role in processing and metabolizing nutrients absorbed from the digestive tract. It provides 8 mg of iron per 100 g, highlighting its nutritional significance. The liver is also responsible for synthesizing very low-density lipoprotein (VLDL) and is integral to lipid metabolism. Additionally, it is the primary site for fructose metabolism, where enzyme deficiencies can impact energy production. However, the liver can be adversely affected by metastases from malignant pancreatic tumors, indicating its susceptibility to cancer spread in patients with such conditions. Overall, Higado is essential for various metabolic processes and is a key organ in maintaining overall health."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DE VERNE-MORRISON:The Verner-Morrison syndrome is another name for VIPoma, characterized by severe diarrhea, hypokalemia, and achlorhydria."}{"title": "DIARREA ACUOSA:Diarrea acuosa is a common condition frequently caused by viral or bacterial infections, and it is characterized by the presence of watery stools. This clinical symptom can also manifest in patients with a congenital deficit of saccharase-isomaltase, particularly upon the intake of sucrose. Additionally, watery diarrhea is a significant symptom associated with VIPoma, a type of tumor that can lead to considerable fluid loss and subsequent metabolic complications."}{"title": "TUMOR PANCRE\u00c1TICO:TUMOR PANCRE\u00c1TICO refers to a type of cancer that affects the pancreas, which is a vital organ involved in digestion and blood sugar regulation. This condition often leads to complications such as hyperglycemia, a condition characterized by elevated blood sugar levels, and malnutrition due to the pancreas's impaired ability to produce digestive enzymes. Additionally, pancreatic tumors can be neuroendocrine in nature, which may result in specific syndromes such as VIPoma, a rare tumor that secretes vasoactive intestinal peptide (VIP) and can cause severe diarrhea and electrolyte imbalances. Overall, TUMOR PANCRE\u00c1TICO encompasses a range of tumor types and associated complications that significantly impact the health and well-being of affected individuals."}{"title": "HIPOPOATASEMIA:Hypokalemia is a condition characterized by low potassium levels, often seen in patients with VIPoma due to excessive diarrhea."}{"title": "ACIDIFICACI\u00d3N METAB\u00d3LICA:Metabolic acidosis is a condition that can arise from the severe fluid and electrolyte loss in VIPoma patients.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "CMT:CMT refers to medullary thyroid carcinoma, a type of cancer that arises from the parafollicular C cells of the thyroid gland."}{"title": "FEO:FEO refers to pheochromocytoma, a tumor of the adrenal gland that can cause excessive production of catecholamines, often associated with MEN2 syndromes."}{"title": "E805K:E805K is a mutation in the RET proto-oncogene that is associated with the development of medullary thyroid carcinoma and is included in the risk stratification for MEN2A."}{"title": "Y806C:Y806C is a mutation in the RET proto-oncogene linked to the risk of medullary thyroid carcinoma and is part of the recommendations for surgical intervention in MEN2A."}{"title": "S904C:S904C is a mutation in the RET proto-oncogene that is associated with MEN2A and influences the clinical management of patients with this condition."}{"title": "NIVELES DE RIESGO:Niveles de riesgo refers to the classification of RET mutations into different risk categories for developing medullary thyroid carcinoma and other associated conditions."}{"title": "CRIBADO BIOQU\u00cdMICO:Cribado bioqu\u00edmico refers to biochemical screening for conditions such as pheochromocytoma and hyperparathyroidism in patients with MEN syndromes."}{"title": "M918T:"}{"title": "RET PROTO-ONCOGENE:The RET proto-oncogene is crucial for the development of MEN2 syndromes, with different mutations associated with varying risks of tumor development."}{"title": "WELLS ET AL.:Wells and colleagues revised the American Thyroid Association guidelines for the management of medullary thyroid carcinoma, contributing to the understanding of thyroid cancer management."}{"title": "VALD\u00c9S GALLEGO:"}{"title": "HYPERPARATHYROIDISM PRIMARIO:Primary hyperparathyroidism is a condition often associated with MEN1 and MEN2 syndromes, characterized by excessive secretion of parathyroid hormone."}{"title": "MICROADENOMA HIPOFISARIO:Microadenoma hipofisario is a small tumor located on the pituitary gland. It is noteworthy that the patient's mother had a microadenoma hipofisario, which was successfully resolved with treatment. This type of tumor can produce hormones, including prolactin, and is frequently examined in relation to multiple endocrine neoplasia (MEN) syndromes."}{"title": "SINDROME MEN1:MEN1 syndrome is characterized by the triad of primary hyperparathyroidism, pituitary tumors, and pancreatic endocrine tumors."}{"title": "SINDROME MEN3:MEN3 is another name for MEN2B syndrome, which is characterized by aggressive medullary thyroid carcinoma and other specific features."}{"title": "FENOTIPO MARFANOIDE:Marfanoid phenotype refers to a set of physical characteristics that may be associated with MEN2B syndrome, including skeletal deformities and laxity of joints."}{"title": "NEUROMAS MUCOSOS:Mucosal neuromas are a characteristic feature of MEN2B syndrome, often found on the lips and tongue."}{"title": "GANGLIONEUROMATOSIS:Ganglioneuromatosis is a condition associated with MEN2B syndrome, characterized by the presence of ganglioneuromas in various tissues.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "MEN4:MEN4 is a newly identified clinical entity similar to MEN1, characterized by mutations in the CDKN1B gene, affecting a small percentage of patients."}{"title": "AIRE:AIRE is a gene linked to autoimmune polyglandular syndrome type 1, which involves multiple autoimmune disorders."}{"title": "ARNOLD A.:Arnold A. is an author who has contributed to the understanding of multiple endocrine neoplasia type 1 and its genetics."}{"title": "VALD\u00c9S GALLEGO N.:Vald\u00e9s Gallego N. is an author known for his contributions to the field of endocrinology and nutrition. He has authored a manual that focuses on endocrine neoplasia, with a specific emphasis on multiple endocrine neoplasia. His work in the \"Manual de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n\" highlights his expertise and dedication to advancing knowledge in these important areas of health."}{"title": "LITIASIS RENAL:LITIASIS RENAL, also known as kidney stones or renal lithiasis, is a medical condition characterized by the formation of solid mineral and salt deposits in the kidneys. This condition affects approximately 5-15% of the population and can lead to significant morbidity and healthcare costs. The formation of kidney stones can be influenced by various factors, including the concentration of solutes in the urine, dietary habits, hydration levels, and metabolic disorders. High calcium levels in the urine, hyperuricemia, and metabolic syndrome are also associated with the development of this condition. Litiasis renal can cause considerable pain and complications in health, making it a significant urological pathology that requires attention and management."}{"title": "HIPERPARATIROIDISMO:Hiperparatiroidismo es una alteraci\u00f3n hormonal que puede afectar a pacientes con insuficiencia renal, influyendo en su nutrici\u00f3n. Esta condici\u00f3n, tambi\u00e9n conocida como hyperparathyroidism, es un trastorno que puede presentarse en individuos con enfermedad renal cr\u00f3nica, lo que requiere intervenciones nutricionales espec\u00edficas para manejar sus efectos."}{"title": "D:D is a hypothetical patient who presents with symptoms and a medical history suggestive of Multiple Endocrine Neoplasia type 1 (MEN1). In addition to being a clinical case study, D also serves as a response option in the context of the questions presented in the modules. This dual role highlights D's significance in both medical education and the understanding of MEN1."}{"title": "TNE:TNE refers to neuroendocrine tumors, which can be non-functioning and are often associated with MEN1."}{"title": "GASTRINOMAS:Gastrinomas are a type of neuroendocrine tumor characterized by the secretion of gastrin, a hormone that stimulates gastric acid production. These tumors are often located in the duodenum and are commonly associated with Zollinger-Ellison syndrome, a condition marked by excessive gastric acid secretion leading to recurrent peptic ulcers. Additionally, gastrinomas can be linked to Multiple Endocrine Neoplasia type 1 (MEN1), a genetic disorder that affects the endocrine glands."}{"title": "NEUROENDOCRINE TUMOR:Neuroendocrine tumors (NETs) are a diverse group of tumors that originate from neuroendocrine cells, which are specialized cells that produce hormones. One specific type of neuroendocrine tumor is found in the pancreas, where it affects the hormone-producing cells, leading to significant health complications. These tumors can be associated with various syndromes, including Multiple Endocrine Neoplasia type 1 (MEN1), highlighting their complex nature and potential for systemic effects."}{"title": "ANALYTICS:Analytics refers to the medical tests and evaluations performed to assess the patient's condition, including hormone levels."}{"title": "MACROADENOMA HIPOFISARIO:Macroadenoma hipofisario refers to a large pituitary adenoma that produces prolactin, commonly seen in patients with MEN1."}{"title": "PROTOONCOGEN RET:Protooncogen RET is a gene that, when mutated, can lead to MEN2, and its study is important in the context of MEN syndromes."}{"title": "ENETS:The European Neuroendocrine Tumor Society (ENETS) is an organization that provides guidelines and recommendations for the management of neuroendocrine tumors."}{"title": "CARCINOMA DE COLON:Colon carcinoma, also known as colon cancer, is a type of cancer that affects the colon and can lead to gastrointestinal bleeding, which may contribute to iron deficiency anemia. It is important to note that patients with Multiple Endocrine Neoplasia type 1 (MEN1) may develop colon carcinoma; however, there is currently no established link between the MEN1 gene and the tumorigenesis of colon carcinoma."}{"title": "GU\u00cdA CL\u00cdNICA DE 2012:The \"GU\u00cdA CL\u00cdNICA DE 2012\" encompasses comprehensive recommendations for the treatment and management of various medical conditions. Specifically, it provides guidelines for the treatment of patients with Zollinger-Ellison syndrome and pancreatic tumors. Additionally, the guidelines address the management of patients with Multiple Endocrine Neoplasia type 1 (MEN1), detailing when surgical interventions should be considered. Overall, the 2012 Clinical Guidelines serve as a crucial resource for healthcare professionals in the effective treatment of these complex conditions."}{"title": "ZOLLINGER-ELLISON SYNDROME:Zollinger-Ellison syndrome is a medical condition characterized by the presence of gastrin-secreting tumors, which result in excessive production of gastric acid. This overproduction can lead to various symptoms, including diarrhea and the development of peptic ulcers. The management of Zollinger-Ellison syndrome often involves surgical intervention, as highlighted in clinical guidelines, emphasizing the importance of addressing the underlying tumors to alleviate the associated symptoms and complications."}{"title": "DREIJERINK KM:Dreijerink KM is an author of a referenced study on breast-cancer predisposition in multiple endocrine neoplasia type 1."}{"title": "VALD\u00c9S GALLEGO N:Vald\u00e9s Gallego N is an author of a referenced manual on endocrinology and nutrition."}{"title": "GASTRINA:Gastrina is a hormone produced by G cells in the stomach, primarily responsible for stimulating the secretion of gastric acid. It plays a crucial role in the digestive process and is often found to be elevated in patients with gastrinomas, which are tumors that secrete excessive amounts of this hormone. Additionally, gastrin may influence intestinal motility, further contributing to its importance in gastrointestinal function."}{"title": "TEST DE SECRETINA:The secretin test is a functional test used to diagnose gastrinomas by measuring the level of gastrin in response to secretin administration."}{"title": "HORMONAS GASTROINTESTINALES:HORMONAS GASTROINTESTINALES, or gastrointestinal hormones, are a group of hormones that play a crucial role in regulating various functions within the digestive system. One notable hormone in this category is gastrin, which is particularly significant in the context of gastrinomas, a type of tumor that secretes excessive amounts of gastrin. These hormones are integral to the digestive process, and their levels and functions were evaluated in patients to identify any abnormalities that may affect digestion."}{"title": "INHIBIDORES DE LA BOMBA DE PROTONES:Los inhibidores de la bomba de protones son medicamentos que reducen la producci\u00f3n de \u00e1cido en el est\u00f3mago y se utilizan en el tratamiento de diversas condiciones, como el s\u00edndrome de Zollinger-Ellison. Estos medicamentos tambi\u00e9n se han probado en pacientes para tratar la regurgitaci\u00f3n. Sin embargo, es importante tener en cuenta que su uso puede estar relacionado con la producci\u00f3n de diarrea."}{"title": "GASTRINOMA PANCRE\u00c1TICO:Pancreatic gastrinomas are gastrin-secreting tumors that can occur in the pancreas, contributing to the symptoms of Zollinger-Ellison syndrome."}{"title": "MIGUEL A. RUBIO HERRERA:Miguel A. Rubio Herrera is a licensed physician and a specialist in Endocrinology and Nutrition. He currently holds the position of Head of the Clinical Nutrition and Dietetics Section at Hospital Cl\u00ednico San Carlos in Madrid. As a medical professional, he focuses on the fields of endocrinology and nutrition, contributing to the healthcare services at the San Carlos Clinical University Hospital in Madrid."}{"title": "UNIVERSIDAD COMPLUTENSE DE MADRID:Universidad Complutense de Madrid is the university where Miguel A. Rubio Herrera completed his doctorate in 1989 and is currently an associate professor."}{"title": "SEEDO:SEEDO, or Sociedad Espa\u00f1ola para el Estudio de la Obesidad, is a prominent organization dedicated to addressing obesity in Spain. It plays a crucial role in establishing therapeutic intervention criteria for obesity and is actively involved in developing consensus guidelines regarding obesity treatment. SEEDO supports the implementation of hypocaloric diets, particularly those based on the Mediterranean diet, recognizing their health benefits in the management of obesity. Through its initiatives, SEEDO aims to promote effective strategies for obesity prevention and treatment, contributing to the overall health of the population."}{"title": "NAOS:NAOS is a strategy developed for addressing obesity in Spain, in which Miguel A. Rubio Herrera has participated."}{"title": "DRECE:DRECE is a study focused on the epidemiology of cardiovascular risk in Spain, in which Miguel A. Rubio Herrera has been involved."}{"title": "MANUAL DE OBESIDAD M\u00d3RBIDA:Manual de Obesidad m\u00f3rbida is a book published by Miguel A. Rubio Herrera, focusing on morbid obesity."}{"title": "THOMPSON:Thompson is referenced as the developer of a surgical technique for treating gastrinomas, specifically duodenotomy plus distal pancreatectomy."}{"title": "PANCREATODUODENECTOM\u00cdA:Pancreatoduodenectomy is a surgical technique recommended for treating gastrinomas, which involves the removal of the pancreas and duodenum."}{"title": "TUMORES PANCRE\u00c1TICOS:Pancreatic tumors are a significant concern in the context of gastrinomas and are discussed in relation to surgical treatment options."}{"title": "MET\u00c1STASIS HEP\u00c1TICAS:Hepatic metastases are a potential complication of gastrinomas, occurring in a percentage of patients and influencing treatment decisions."}{"title": "MET\u00c1STASIS GANGLIONARES:Lymph node metastases are a common issue in patients with gastrinomas, complicating treatment and prognosis.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "SED:The SED is a professional organization that focuses on diabetes, having previously worked on optimizing diabetes management."}{"title": "ENRICA:The ENRICA study is a research project conducted between 2008-2010 to assess obesity prevalence in Spain, involving a representative sample of the population."}{"title": "ENPE:ENPE is an organization dedicated to studying obesity prevalence and its impact on public health. One of its significant initiatives is the ENPE study, a research project conducted between 2014 and 2015, which aimed to evaluate obesity prevalence within a specific age group in Spain. Through its research efforts, ENPE seeks to contribute valuable insights into the public health challenges posed by obesity."}{"title": "ASTURIAS:Asturias is an autonomous community located in northern Spain, distinguished by several notable characteristics. It is recognized for a higher occurrence of RTFQ gene mutations and has high rates of obesity among its population. The region is also known for its aging demographic, which significantly influences diabetes statistics in neighboring areas. In terms of healthcare, Asturias is home to prominent institutions, including the Hospital Universitario Central de Asturias and the University Hospital Central of Asturias, which provide essential medical services to the community. Additionally, patients in Asturias are required to submit a justification report to continue receiving treatment for their nutritional needs, highlighting the region's approach to healthcare management."}{"title": "EXTREMADURA:Extremadura is an autonomous community in Spain known for its unique healthcare policies and demographic health statistics. In this region, patients are required to submit a justification report to continue receiving treatment for their nutritional needs, highlighting the community's structured approach to healthcare management. Additionally, Extremadura boasts lower obesity prevalence rates compared to other regions in Spain, indicating a potentially healthier population in terms of weight-related issues."}{"title": "CANARIAS:Canarias is an autonomous community in Spain known for its significant health challenges, particularly related to diabetes and obesity. The region has been noted for having higher mortality rates associated with diabetes, which is a critical public health concern. Additionally, Canarias has a high prevalence of obesity, further complicating the health landscape of the community. In response to these issues, patients in Canarias are required to submit a justification report to the Patient Care Service of the hospitals within the Canarian Health Service in order to continue receiving treatment for their nutritional needs. This requirement highlights the region's efforts to manage and address the health complications arising from obesity and diabetes."}{"title": "UNITED STATES OF AMERICA:The United States has one of the highest obesity prevalence rates in the world, ranging between 31% and 35%."}{"title": "MEXICO:Mexico is one of the countries with the highest obesity prevalence rates globally, with rates ranging between 31% and 35%. This significant prevalence highlights Mexico's status as a nation facing serious public health challenges related to obesity."}{"title": "EGYPT:Egypt is noted for having high obesity prevalence rates, similar to the United States and Mexico."}{"title": "SAUDI ARABIA:Saudi Arabia is a country characterized by a high prevalence of obesity, with rates estimated to be between 31% and 35%. This places it among the nations with the highest obesity prevalence rates globally."}{"title": "TRASTORNOS ELECTROL\u00cdTICOS:TRASTORNOS ELECTROL\u00cdTICOS refer to electrolyte imbalances in the body, which are significant in the context of health and nutrition. These disorders are often associated with obesity and various metabolic disorders, highlighting their relevance in dietary considerations and overall health management."}{"title": "NEURONAS:Neurons that modulate appetite, including those expressing neuropeptide Y and agouti-related protein, which have orexigenic properties, and melanocortin pathways that are anorexigenic."}{"title": "N\u00daCLEO ARCUATO:The arcuate nucleus is a part of the hypothalamus involved in appetite regulation, communicating with other hypothalamic nuclei."}{"title": "N\u00daCLEOS DORSOMEDIAL, PARAVENTRICULAR, HIPOT\u00c1LAMO LATERAL:These nuclei in the hypothalamus activate the sympathetic and parasympathetic nervous systems in response to appetite signals."}{"title": "LEPTINA:Leptina es una hormona producida por los adipocitos que desempe\u00f1a un papel crucial en la regulaci\u00f3n del apetito y el gasto metab\u00f3lico. Sus niveles est\u00e1n directamente relacionados con la masa grasa corporal, y se ha observado que pueden disminuir en pacientes caqu\u00e9cticos, como aquellos con c\u00e1ncer de es\u00f3fago. Esta hormona no solo ayuda a regular el equilibrio energ\u00e9tico y suprime el hambre, sino que tambi\u00e9n est\u00e1 vinculada a los \u00e1cidos grasos de cadena corta. En el contexto de la obesidad, los niveles de leptina tienden a estar elevados, lo que contribuye a un aumento del tono simp\u00e1tico y a la inflamaci\u00f3n. Adem\u00e1s, la leptina ejerce efectos anorexig\u00e9nicos al estimular las v\u00edas melanocortinas y al inhibir las v\u00edas orexig\u00e9nicas, lo que refuerza su papel en la regulaci\u00f3n del peso corporal."}{"title": "P\u00c9PTIDO YY:Peptide YY is secreted in the distal intestine and primarily has anorexigenic effects, interacting with neuropeptide Y neurons."}{"title": "OBESIDAD METAB\u00d3LICAMENTE SANA:\"OBESIDAD METAB\u00d3LICAMENTE SANA\" refers to a condition characterized by individuals who are classified as obese yet do not display metabolic complications typically associated with obesity. These individuals tend to have a lower percentage of visceral fat and exhibit cardiovascular risk levels comparable to those of healthy individuals with normal weight."}{"title": "NORMOPESO:NORMOPESO refers to individuals who maintain a normal weight and do not experience metabolic complications. This term is associated with achieving a healthy weight, which is particularly important in the nutritional management of patients with chronic kidney disease. Maintaining a normoweight is considered a key goal for promoting overall health and preventing potential health issues related to weight and metabolism."}{"title": "SISTEMA NERVIOSO SIMP\u00c1TICO:The sympathetic nervous system is part of the autonomic nervous system that can influence appetite regulation and energy expenditure."}{"title": "SISTEMA NERVIOSO PARASIMP\u00c1TICO:The parasympathetic nervous system is part of the autonomic nervous system that can also affect appetite and digestion."}{"title": "N\u00daCLEO ACCUMBENS:The nucleus accumbens is a brain region involved in reward and addiction, influencing eating behavior and appetite."}{"title": "AM\u00cdGDALA:The amygdala is a brain region associated with memory and emotions, which can impact appetite and food-related behaviors."}{"title": "C\u00d3RTEX PREFRONTAL:The prefrontal cortex is involved in executive functions and decision-making, including choices related to food intake."}{"title": "NURSES' HEALTH STUDY:The Nurses' Health Study is a long-term epidemiological study that investigates the health effects of diet, lifestyle, and other factors among nurses, with a particular focus on women's health issues. This extensive study has been following over 90,000 women for more than 30 years, providing valuable insights into the association between food consumption, obesity, and various health outcomes. Over its 32-year duration, the Nurses' Health Study has contributed significantly to understanding how diet and lifestyle choices impact women's health."}{"title": "EUROPEAN PROSPECTIVE INVESTIGATION INTO CANCER AND NUTRITION STUDY:The EPIC study is a large-scale research project that investigates the relationships between diet, lifestyle, and health outcomes, including cardiovascular disease, across Europe."}{"title": "EHGNA:EHGNA, or Non-Alcoholic Fatty Liver Disease, is a condition characterized by excessive fat accumulation in the liver without the influence of alcohol consumption. It is closely associated with obesity and various metabolic disorders, impacting a significant percentage of obese individuals. This condition affects a notable portion of the adult population, highlighting its relevance in discussions surrounding obesity and liver health."}{"title": "OBESIDAD METAB\u00d3LICAMENTE ENFERMA:Metabolically unhealthy obesity is characterized by the presence of metabolic complications in individuals who are obese, significantly increasing their risk for cardiovascular disease."}{"title": "RATIO DE HAZARD:Hazard ratio is a measure used in epidemiological studies to compare the risk of a certain event occurring in two groups, often used to assess the impact of obesity on health outcomes."}{"title": "ALLER R:Aller R is an author of a consensus document on the management of non-alcoholic fatty liver disease."}{"title": "FERN\u00c1NDEZ-RODR\u00cdGUEZ C:Fern\u00e1ndez-Rodr\u00edguez C is a co-author of a clinical practice guideline on non-alcoholic fatty liver disease."}{"title": "DIEHL AM:Diehl AM is an author who has contributed to the understanding of the causes and treatment of non-alcoholic steatohepatitis."}{"title": "DAY C:Day C is a co-author of research on the pathogenesis and treatment of non-alcoholic steatohepatitis."}{"title": "POLYZOS SA:Polyzos SA is an author who has researched the relationship between obesity and non-alcoholic fatty liver disease."}{"title": "KOUNTOURAS J:Kountouras J is a co-author of studies on obesity and its impact on liver health."}{"title": "MANTZOROS CS:Mantzoros CS is an author known for his research on the health implications of obesity. He has conducted studies that discuss the relationship between obesity and cancer risk, as well as exploring the connection between obesity and non-alcoholic fatty liver disease. Through his work, Mantzoros CS contributes to the understanding of how obesity can influence various health conditions."}{"title": "STEFAN N:Stefan N is an author who has contributed to the understanding of non-alcoholic fatty liver disease and its treatment strategies."}{"title": "H\u00c4RING HU:H\u00e4iring HU is a co-author of research on the causes and consequences of non-alcoholic fatty liver disease."}{"title": "CUSI K:Cusi K is an author who has studied non-alcoholic fatty liver disease and its implications for health."}{"title": "GASTROENTEROL HEPATOL:GASTROENTEROL HEPATOL is a journal that focuses on the fields of Gastroenterology and Hepatology. It publishes research related to digestive health and liver diseases, contributing to the advancement of knowledge and understanding in these medical specialties."}{"title": "PEPTIDOS NATRIURETICOS:P\u00e9ptidos natriur\u00e9ticos play a role in regulating vascular tone and promoting renal excretion of sodium and water, with beneficial metabolic actions."}{"title": "NEPRILISINA:Neprilysin is an endopeptidase that degrades natriuretic peptides and is overexpressed in adipose tissue, potentially due to hyperinsulinemia and insulin resistance."}{"title": "SISTEMA NERVIOSO SIMPATICO:The sympathetic nervous system is activated in obesity, leading to increased renal sodium retention and fluid volume expansion."}{"title": "FIBROSIS MIOCARDICA:Cardiac fibrosis is a condition exacerbated by obesity and the interactions between leptin, aldosterone, and natriuretic peptides."}{"title": "VOLUMEN SISTOLICO:Increased stroke volume is a hemodynamic change observed in obesity, affecting cardiac function."}{"title": "PRESION ARTERIAL:Elevated blood pressure is a common consequence of obesity, linked to increased aldosterone and sympathetic nervous system activity."}{"title": "GROSOR DE LA PARED DEL VI:Increased left ventricular wall thickness is a structural change associated with obesity and hypertension."}{"title": "HIPERTENSION PULMONAR:Pulmonary hypertension can occur as a complication of obesity, affecting overall cardiovascular health."}{"title": "DISFUNCION DIASTOLICA DEL VI:Diastolic dysfunction of the left ventricle is a cardiac condition that can be exacerbated by obesity."}{"title": "DISFUNCION SISTOLICA DEL VI:Systolic dysfunction of the left ventricle is a potential outcome of obesity-related cardiac changes."}{"title": "FALLO VENTRICULAR DERECHO:Right ventricular failure can be a consequence of obesity and related cardiovascular complications."}{"title": "ADIPONECTINA:Adiponectin is a protein hormone produced by adipose tissue that has anti-inflammatory effects and is often decreased in obesity."}{"title": "VOLUMEN SANGUINEO:"}{"title": "LEGACY:El estudio LEGACY investiga el efecto a largo plazo de la gesti\u00f3n del peso en la fibrilaci\u00f3n auricular."}{"title": "CARDIOFIT:CARDIOFIT is a study that investigates the effects of aerobic exercise on the recurrence of atrial fibrillation (AF) in individuals who have experienced weight loss. The research aims to understand how engaging in aerobic activities can influence the frequency of AF episodes in this specific population. The study highlights the significance of exercise as a potential intervention for managing atrial fibrillation, particularly in those who have successfully lost weight."}{"title": "PACKER M:Packer M is an author and researcher who has investigated the relationship between obesity and atrial fibrillation. His work has contributed to studies examining the impact of obesity and inflammation on the myocardium, highlighting the significant connections between these health issues and their effects on heart rhythm disorders."}{"title": "LAVIE C:Lavie C es un autor que ha estudiado la asociaci\u00f3n entre la grasa epic\u00e1rdica y la fibrilaci\u00f3n auricular."}{"title": "INFLAMACI\u00d3N CARD\u00cdACA:La inflamaci\u00f3n card\u00edaca es una condici\u00f3n que puede contribuir a la insuficiencia card\u00edaca y otros problemas cardiovasculares."}{"title": "ADIPOSIDAD INTRAMIOC\u00c1RDICA:La adiposidad intramioc\u00e1rdica se refiere a la acumulaci\u00f3n de grasa dentro del m\u00fasculo card\u00edaco, que puede afectar la funci\u00f3n card\u00edaca."}{"title": "ADIPOSIDAD VISCERAL:La adiposidad visceral es la acumulaci\u00f3n de grasa en el abdomen, que se asocia con un mayor riesgo de enfermedades cardiovasculares."}{"title": "ADIPOCITOCINAS:Las adipocitocinas son hormonas producidas por el tejido adiposo que pueden afectar el metabolismo y la salud cardiovascular."}{"title": "VEGF-1:VEGF-1 es un factor de crecimiento que promueve la formaci\u00f3n de vasos sangu\u00edneos y puede estar involucrado en la salud cardiovascular."}{"title": "METALOPROTEINASAS:Las metaloproteinasas son enzimas que degradan componentes de la matriz extracelular y pueden influir en la remodelaci\u00f3n card\u00edaca."}{"title": "CICLOS DE PESO:Los ciclos de peso se refieren a las fluctuaciones en el peso corporal, que pueden afectar la salud cardiovascular y la recurrencia de arritmias."}{"title": "CIRUG\u00cdA BARI\u00c1TRICA:CIRUG\u00cdA BARI\u00c1TRICA, or bariatric surgery, is a medical procedure designed to treat severe obesity through various surgical techniques. It is primarily aimed at facilitating weight loss for individuals suffering from obesity, particularly those with related health issues such as diabetes. The procedure is increasingly utilized, especially among diabetic patients, and is associated with low complication rates; however, the risks may increase with more complex interventions.\n\nBariatric surgery is an elective surgical procedure performed on patients with morbid obesity, often involving techniques such as simplified gastric bypass. This surgery not only aids in significant weight loss but also contributes to the improvement of comorbidities, including better management of type 2 diabetes and potential positive effects on conditions like atrial fibrillation.\n\nBefore and after the surgery, patients are required to adhere to specific dietary management protocols to optimize outcomes. Overall, bariatric surgery serves as an effective treatment option for severe obesity, helping individuals achieve substantial weight loss and enhance their overall health."}{"title": "LEGACY STUDY:The LEGACY Study investigates the long-term effects of goal-directed weight management in patients with atrial fibrillation."}{"title": "INTERNATIONAL AGENCY FOR RESEARCH ON CANCER:The IARC is an organization that assesses cancer risks associated with various factors, including obesity."}{"title": "WORLD CANCER RESEARCH FUND:The World Cancer Research Fund (WCRF) is an organization dedicated to cancer prevention, emphasizing the importance of diet and lifestyle factors, including obesity. It conducts research to understand how these elements influence cancer risk and promotes awareness of the role that diet and physical activity play in reducing the likelihood of developing cancer. Through its efforts, the WCRF aims to provide valuable insights and guidance for healthier living to help prevent cancer."}{"title": "ATRIAL FIBRILLATION:Atrial fibrillation (AF) is a common heart condition that can lead to serious complications, including stroke."}{"title": "CANCER PREVENTION-II:Cancer Prevention-II is a study that investigates the relationship between obesity and cancer mortality rates. It aims to examine how obesity may influence the likelihood of cancer-related deaths, providing valuable insights into the potential impact of weight management on cancer outcomes."}{"title": "ENDOMETRIUM:The endometrium is the inner lining of the uterus, playing a crucial role in the reproductive system. It is important to note that obesity is a significant risk factor for endometrial cancer, highlighting the health implications associated with the condition of the endometrium."}{"title": "OVARY:The ovary is a female reproductive organ, and obesity increases the risk of ovarian cancer."}{"title": "PULM\u00d3N:Pulm\u00f3n refers to the lungs, which are vital organs in the respiratory system. Obesity is associated with a higher risk of lung cancer, highlighting the impact of body weight on lung health. Additionally, the lungs can be a site for carcinoid tumors, which primarily originate in the digestive system but can also manifest in the pulmonary region. This underscores the importance of understanding the various health risks associated with the lungs, particularly in relation to obesity and tumor development."}{"title": "SWEDISH OBESE SUBJECTS:Swedish obese subjects are individuals studied to understand the relationship between obesity and new-onset atrial fibrillation."}{"title": "EE. UU.:EE. UU. (United States) is a country where a significant percentage of cancer mortality is attributed to obesity."}{"title": "AVGERINOS KI:Avgerinos KI is an author of a study discussing the relationship between obesity and cancer risk."}{"title": "SPYROU N:Spyrou N is an author of a study discussing the relationship between obesity and cancer risk."}{"title": "DALAMAGA M:Dalamaga M is an author of a study discussing the relationship between obesity and cancer risk."}{"title": "CALLE EE:Calle EE is an author of a study that provides epidemiological evidence on overweight, obesity, and cancer."}{"title": "KAAKS R:Kaaks R is an author of a study that provides epidemiological evidence on overweight, obesity, and cancer."}{"title": "LAUBY-SECRETAN B:Lauby-Secretan B is an author of a study discussing body fatness and cancer."}{"title": "CARCINOMA ESOF\u00c1GICO:Carcinoma esof\u00e1gico is a type of cancer that occurs in the esophagus, associated with various risk factors including obesity."}{"title": "C\u00c1NCER COLORRECTAL:C\u00e1ncer colorrectal, or colorectal cancer, is a type of cancer that affects the colon and rectum. Its incidence has been linked to various dietary factors and lifestyle choices. Research indicates that the consumption of legumes may reduce the risk of developing adenomas and carcinomas associated with this cancer. Additionally, a higher intake of dietary fiber and whole grains has been shown to lower the risk of colorectal cancer, suggesting that fiber plays a protective role through various proposed mechanisms.\n\nObesity is identified as a contributing risk factor for colorectal cancer, highlighting the importance of maintaining a healthy weight. Furthermore, the consumption of omega-3 fatty acids has also been associated with a reduced risk of this disease. Conversely, a high intake of red and processed meats has been linked to an increased risk of colorectal adenomas, emphasizing the negative impact of certain dietary choices.\n\nThe relationship between colorectal cancer and the consumption of fruits and vegetables is noted to be inversely related, although the evidence supporting this connection is considered modest. Overall, dietary habits, including the intake of fiber, legumes, and omega-3 fatty acids, alongside lifestyle factors such as obesity, play significant roles in the risk of developing c\u00e1ncer colorrectal."}{"title": "MELANOMA M\u00daLTIPLE:Mieloma m\u00faltiple is a type of blood cancer that has been studied in relation to obesity."}{"title": "MENINGIOMA:Meningioma is a type of brain tumor that has been associated with obesity."}{"title": "BUPROPION-NALTREXONE:Bupropion-naltrexone is a combination pharmacotherapy used for weight loss, particularly effective in patients with appetite control issues."}{"title": "BILLIES SK:Billes SK is an author who contributed to the research on naltrexone/bupropion for obesity."}{"title": "GASTRECTOMY VERTICAL:Gastrectomy vertical is a surgical technique for weight loss that involves the removal of a portion of the stomach."}{"title": "BYPASS G\u00c1STRICO:BYPASS G\u00c1STRICO is a type of weight-loss surgery that involves altering the digestive system to assist patients in losing weight. This mixed surgical technique reduces the size of the stomach and modifies the digestive process, creating a small pouch from the stomach that is directly connected to the small intestine. While effective for weight loss, bypass g\u00e1strico can lead to complications similar to those associated with biliopancreatic diversion, particularly when performed distally or using pure restrictive techniques. Additionally, it is often linked with the dumping syndrome, a condition that can occur after the surgery. Overall, bypass g\u00e1strico is recognized as a bariatric surgery aimed at promoting significant weight loss through these surgical modifications."}{"title": "CRUCE DUODENAL:Cruce duodenal is a malabsorptive surgical technique designed to assist in weight loss, particularly for individuals suffering from severe obesity. The procedure involves a two-step process that includes a longitudinal gastrectomy, which is performed while preserving the pylorus. This approach aims to reduce the stomach's capacity and alter the digestive process, thereby promoting weight loss and improving overall health outcomes for patients."}{"title": "HORMONA ESTIMULANTE DE MELANOCITOS:Hormona estimulante de melanocitos (\u03b1-MSH) is a hormone involved in the regulation of appetite and energy balance."}{"title": "PROOPIOMELANOCORTINA:Proopiomelanocortina (POMC) is a precursor protein that is involved in the production of several hormones that regulate appetite."}{"title": "CRISIS COMICIALES:Crisis comiciales refer to seizure episodes that can occur in patients with adrenoleukodystrophy and may also serve as a contraindication for certain medications, such as bupropion."}{"title": "NALTREXONE:Naltrexone is a medication that functions by blocking opioid receptors in the body. It is primarily used in combination with bupropion, a medication that is also associated with weight loss. Research has focused on the effects of this combination on weight loss and its potential benefits in addressing obesity-related risk factors."}{"title": "GASTRECTOM\u00cdA VERTICAL:Gastrectom\u00eda vertical, also known as vertical gastrectomy, is a surgical procedure designed primarily for weight loss, particularly in patients suffering from severe obesity. This procedure involves the vertical removal of a portion of the stomach, which effectively reduces its size and aids in weight management. By decreasing the stomach's capacity, gastrectom\u00eda vertical helps patients achieve significant weight loss and addresses obesity-related health issues."}{"title": "AHMAD A:Ahmad A es un autor que ha investigado la prevalencia del s\u00edndrome de dumping tras la gastrectom\u00eda vertical."}{"title": "KORNICH DB:Kornich DB es un autor que ha colaborado en la investigaci\u00f3n sobre el s\u00edndrome de dumping y su prevalencia tras la cirug\u00eda bari\u00e1trica."}{"title": "KRASNER H:Krasner H es un autor que ha contribuido a estudios sobre el s\u00edndrome de dumping en pacientes postquir\u00fargicos."}{"title": "ECKARDT S:Eckardt S es un autor que ha participado en la investigaci\u00f3n sobre el s\u00edndrome de dumping y su manejo."}{"title": "AHMAD Z:Ahmad Z es un autor que ha coescrito sobre la prevalencia del s\u00edndrome de dumping tras la cirug\u00eda bari\u00e1trica."}{"title": "BRASLOW A:Braslow A es un autor que ha colaborado en estudios sobre el s\u00edndrome de dumping y su prevalencia."}{"title": "VAN BEEK AP:Van Beek AP es un autor que ha investigado el s\u00edndrome de dumping tras diversas cirug\u00edas gastrointestinales."}{"title": "EMOUS M:Emous M es un autor que ha contribuido a la investigaci\u00f3n sobre el s\u00edndrome de dumping y su tratamiento."}{"title": "LAVILLE M:Laville M es un autor que ha participado en estudios sobre el s\u00edndrome de dumping y su manejo cl\u00ednico."}{"title": "TACK J:Tack J es un autor que ha investigado el s\u00edndrome de dumping y su fisiopatolog\u00eda."}{"title": "ANASTOMOSIS GASTROYEYUNAL:La anastomosis gastroyeyunal es una conexi\u00f3n quir\u00fargica entre el est\u00f3mago y el yeyuno, que puede influir en el vaciamiento g\u00e1strico y el s\u00edndrome de dumping."}{"title": "NEUROGLUCOPENIA:La neuroglucopenia es una condici\u00f3n que ocurre cuando hay una falta de glucosa en el cerebro, lo que puede provocar s\u00edntomas como confusi\u00f3n y mareos, a menudo relacionada con hipoglucemias."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROMA DE DUMPING:"}{"title": "MIFFLIN-ST. JEOR:The Mifflin-St. Jeor equation is a more accurate method for estimating energy requirements, particularly for individuals with obesity."}{"title": "DUMPING SYNDROME:Dumping syndrome is a condition that can occur after certain types of gastric surgery, characterized by rapid gastric emptying and various symptoms."}{"title": "WOMAN:A 50-year-old woman weighing 85 kg and 1.60 m tall, seeking consultation for weight loss."}{"title": "NIFEDIPINO:Nifedipino is a calcium antagonist primarily used to treat high blood pressure and angina. It is also utilized in cases of late dumping syndrome, although its effectiveness can vary among individuals."}{"title": "REFERENCIAS:References cited in the text provide evidence and studies related to dumping syndrome and its management."}{"title": "DIAZ\u00d3XIDO:"}{"title": "PERREAULT L.:Perreault L. es un autor que ha contribuido a la literatura sobre la terapia diet\u00e9tica para la obesidad en adultos."}{"title": "KUNINS L.:Kunins L. es un editor que ha colaborado en la obra de UpToDate sobre la obesidad en adultos."}{"title": "BMI:BMI, or Body Mass Index, is a widely used measure that assesses an individual's body weight in relation to their height. This calculation helps categorize individuals into different classifications: underweight, normal weight, overweight, or obese. BMI serves as an important tool in evaluating nutritional status and can influence the nutritional support needs of patients. It is commonly utilized in obesity and health assessments to provide insights into an individual's weight status, thereby aiding in the identification of potential health risks associated with being underweight or overweight."}{"title": "LOW-FAT DIET:A low-fat diet is a dietary plan that restricts fat intake, often used for weight loss and health improvement."}{"title": "LOW-CARBOHYDRATE DIET:A low-carbohydrate diet is a dietary plan that limits carbohydrate intake, aimed at weight loss and managing blood sugar levels."}{"title": "BARIATRIC SURGERY:Bariatric surgery is a medical procedure designed for weight loss through various surgical techniques that modify the digestive system. This includes methods such as gastrectomy and bypass surgery. It is primarily recommended for individuals suffering from obesity and related health issues, including Type 2 diabetes, as it aims to achieve significant weight loss and improve metabolic health. \n\nThe procedure is recognized as the most effective treatment for patients with morbid obesity, leading to various physiological changes, including hormonal alterations and modifications in intestinal microbiota that contribute to weight loss. However, bariatric surgery also necessitates specific dietary adjustments post-operation and is associated with potential complications and nutritional issues. \n\nFurthermore, bariatric surgery is linked to various health outcomes, including impacts on cardiovascular disease and mortality rates among patients with obesity. It is often discussed in the context of Enhanced Recovery After Surgery (ERAS) protocols, which are designed to enhance recovery and minimize complications following the procedure. Overall, bariatric surgery encompasses a range of surgical interventions aimed at facilitating weight loss and improving overall health in individuals with obesity."}{"title": "GARDNER CD:"}{"title": "CUMMINGS DE:Cummings DE is a researcher who has contributed to the understanding of metabolic surgery for the treatment of Type 2 diabetes in obese individuals."}{"title": "RUBINO F:Rubino F is a researcher known for his work on metabolic surgery and its effects on Type 2 diabetes management."}{"title": "RAMOS-LEVI AM:Ramos-Levi AM is a researcher who specializes in statistical modeling aimed at predicting the remission of Type 2 diabetes following bariatric surgery. In addition to their research work, Ramos-Levi AM has authored multiple studies that focus on the relationship between diabetes remission and bariatric surgery, contributing valuable insights to the field."}{"title": "METABOLIC SURGERY:Metabolic surgery refers to surgical procedures aimed at inducing weight loss and improving metabolic conditions, particularly in patients with obesity and Type 2 diabetes."}{"title": "CEFALU WT:Cefalu WT is an author of a study discussing the definition of diabetes cure published in Diabetes Care in 2009."}{"title": "CERIELLO A:Ceriello A is an author of a study discussing the definition of diabetes cure published in Diabetes Care in 2009."}{"title": "DEL PRATO S:Del Prato S is an author of a study discussing the definition of diabetes cure published in Diabetes Care in 2009."}{"title": "INZUCCHI SE:Inzucchi SE is a notable author recognized for their contributions to the field of diabetes care. In 2009, they authored a study published in Diabetes Care that discusses the definition of a diabetes cure. Additionally, Inzucchi SE played a significant role in developing management guidelines for diabetes care, further emphasizing their expertise and commitment to improving diabetes treatment and understanding."}{"title": "MATIA P:Matia P is an author of a study on statistical models predicting type 2 diabetes remission after bariatric surgery."}{"title": "CABRERIZO L:Cabrerizo L is an author of a study on statistical models predicting type 2 diabetes remission after bariatric surgery."}{"title": "BARABASH A:Barabash A is an author of a study on statistical models predicting type 2 diabetes remission after bariatric surgery."}{"title": "SANCHEZ-PERNAUTE A:Sanchez-Pernaute A is an author of a study on statistical models predicting type 2 diabetes remission after bariatric surgery."}{"title": "CALLE-PASCUAL AL:Calle-Pascual AL is an author of a study on statistical models predicting type 2 diabetes remission after bariatric surgery."}{"title": "TYPE 2 DIABETES REMISSION:Type 2 diabetes remission refers to the state where diabetes symptoms are no longer present, often discussed in the context of bariatric surgery outcomes."}{"title": "SUSTAIN TRIALS:The SUSTAIN trials are a series of clinical studies evaluating the efficacy and safety of semaglutide in the treatment of type 2 diabetes."}{"title": "SEMAGLUTIDE:Semaglutide is a medication used for the treatment of type 2 diabetes, showing significant improvements in HbA1c and weight loss."}{"title": "LIRAGLUTIDE:Liraglutide is a human glucagon-like peptide-1 analog that has been extensively studied for its efficacy and safety in the management of weight and the treatment of diabetes. It is commonly used as an injectable medication for controlling type 2 diabetes. In clinical studies, liraglutide is often compared with another medication, semaglutide, highlighting its role in diabetes treatment."}{"title": "DERIVACI\u00d3N BILIOPANCRE\u00c1TICA:Derivaci\u00f3n biliopancre\u00e1tica, also known as biliopancreatic diversion, is a surgical technique designed for weight loss that significantly alters the digestive system to assist patients in achieving substantial weight reduction. This procedure has demonstrated high success rates, particularly among individuals classified as superobese. It combines elements of gastric bypass with biliopancreatic diversion to enhance malabsorption, thereby promoting effective weight loss."}{"title": "AHMANN A:Ahmann A is a co-author of the study discussing the comparative efficacy of semaglutide in diabetes treatment."}{"title": "CARIOU B:Cariou B is a researcher involved in the studies on semaglutide and its effects on diabetes management."}{"title": "CHOW F:Chow F is one of the authors contributing to the research on semaglutide's efficacy in diabetes treatment."}{"title": "DAVIES MJ:Davies MJ is a prominent researcher and co-author involved in multiple studies related to type 2 diabetes. They have contributed to the evaluation of semaglutide, a medication used for managing this condition. Additionally, Davies MJ played a significant role in the SCALE Diabetes randomized clinical trial, which focused on assessing the efficacy of liraglutide for weight loss in patients with type 2 diabetes. Furthermore, Davies MJ has conducted a systematic review and meta-analysis examining the relationship between fruit and vegetable intake and type 2 diabetes, highlighting their commitment to advancing research in this field."}{"title": "J\u00d3DAR E:J\u00f3dar E is a researcher mentioned in the context of the semaglutide studies."}{"title": "PRATLEY RE:Pratley RE is a researcher who has made significant contributions to the field of diabetes treatment, particularly focusing on type 2 diabetes mellitus in older adults. Additionally, Pratley RE is one of the authors involved in the SUSTAIN trials, which compare the efficacy of semaglutide and dulaglutide, two medications used in the management of this condition. Through these efforts, Pratley RE has played a vital role in advancing the understanding and treatment options for diabetes in the aging population."}{"title": "L\u00dcDEMANN J:L\u00fcdemann J is a co-author of the SUSTAIN 7 study on semaglutide."}{"title": "ANDREASSEN C:Andreassen C is a researcher associated with the SUSTAIN trials."}{"title": "NAVARRIA A:Navarria A is one of the authors of the studies on semaglutide."}{"title": "BUCHWALD H:Buchwald H is a researcher referenced in the systematic review and meta-analysis of bariatric surgery."}{"title": "AVIDOR Y:Avidor Y is a co-author of the systematic review on bariatric surgery outcomes."}{"title": "BRAUNWALD E:Braunwald E is a researcher involved in the systematic review of bariatric surgery."}{"title": "JENSEN MD:Jensen MD is one of the authors of the systematic review on bariatric surgery."}{"title": "PORIES W:Pories W is a co-author of the systematic review discussing bariatric surgery outcomes."}{"title": "FAHRBACH K:Fahrbach K is a researcher mentioned in the systematic review of bariatric surgery."}{"title": "CHANG SH:Chang SH is a co-author of the updated systematic review and meta-analysis on bariatric surgery."}{"title": "STOLL CR:Stoll CR is a researcher involved in the updated systematic review of bariatric surgery."}{"title": "SONG J:Song J is one of the authors of the updated systematic review on bariatric surgery."}{"title": "VARELA JE:Varela JE is a co-author of the updated systematic review discussing the effectiveness of bariatric surgery."}¨1␀␀␀␀␀	1␀␀␀␀␀¿	1␀␀␀␀␀€	1␀␀␀␀␀91␀␀␀␀␀Ê1␀␀␀␀␀Ë1␀␀␀␀␀å1␀␀␀␀␀_1␀␀␀␀␀ﬁ1␀␀␀␀␀§1␀␀␀␀␀µ1␀␀␀␀␀g1␀␀␀␀␀1␀␀␀␀␀1␀␀␀␀␀Ω